{"type":"system","subtype":"task_notification","task_id":"adcc63896c02e476b","tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_015BB6g31p2CBoUKBhiJXNKM","status":"completed","output_file":"/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-agent-LlK7ZE/tmp/claude-31072124/-local-home-scheschb--harvest-work-harvest-work-RqaJY6/b566403e-4c11-4a9b-ad3a-d43b1f08afd2/tasks/adcc63896c02e476b.output","summary":"Both artifacts written, numbering verified contiguous with no gaps.\n\n**Files**\n- `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-RqaJY6/translation/phaseA/errors_4.md` — **24 rows** (4.1–4.24)\n- `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-RqaJY6/translation/phaseA/configs_4.md` — **182 rows** (4.1–4.182)\n\n**Key findings from reading the sources**\n\n- Every HMAC `*_verify` returns `crypto_verify_N(h, correct) | (-(h == correct)) | sodium_memcmp(correct, h, N)` — three OR-terms: a constant-time compare, a *pointer-aliasing guard* that forces `-1` if `h` aliases the internal stack buffer (dead in practice but semantically a forced rejection), and a redundant second constant-time compare. `crypto_onetimeauth_poly1305_donna_verify` is different: it uses **only** `crypto_verify_16`, with no memcmp and no aliasing guard. Compare widths differ per primitive (32 / 64 / 32 / 16).\n- The only `sodium_misuse()` sites are in `crypto_auth_hmacsha256_init` and `crypto_auth_hmacsha512_init` (the latter reached by `hmacsha512256_init`, which is a pure cast-and-delegate). Trigger is `key == NULL && 0 < keylen <= BLOCKBYTES`. `sodium_misuse()` never returns (handler then `abort()`), so it is not an `int` error.\n- Two asymmetries worth flagging for the port: `key == NULL && keylen == 0` is **legal** and returns 0 (HMAC over an all-zero key), while `key == NULL && keylen > BLOCKBYTES` skips the misuse check entirely and dereferences NULL inside `crypto_hash_*_update` — undefined behaviour, not a defined `-1`.\n- The keylen branch boundary is strictly `>` (`> 64` for sha256, `> 128` for sha512): `keylen == BLOCKBYTES` is **not** hashed. Hashing forces `keylen` to 32 / 64.\n- All non-`verify` entry points in this area unconditionally `return 0`; there are no length or NULL validations anywhere (only `__attribute__((nonnull))` header hints), so the entire error surface is the verify paths plus the two abort branches.\n- `crypto_auth_hmacsha512_KEYBYTES` is 32 even though the tag is 64 — `crypto_auth_hmacsha512_keygen` writes 32 bytes.\n- `hmacsha512256_final` truncates to the first 32 bytes of the SHA-512 HMAC and zeroes `out0`; its state is a `typedef` of `crypto_auth_hmacsha512_state`, so cross-API state interop is a real (testable) configuration.\n- Build config confirmed: no `HAVE_TI_MODE` / `HAVE_EMMINTRIN_H`, so poly1305 uses `donna` with `poly1305_donna32.h` (26-bit limbs, `poly1305_block_size == 16`), `sse2/` is not compiled, `_pick_best_implementation` degenerates to re-installing donna and returning 0, and `crypto_verify_n` / `sodium_memcmp` take their portable branches.\n- The donna `poly1305_update` leftover logic has three independently reachable branches per call (fill-leftover-and-flush, full-block, store-remainder); configs 4.165–4.169 enumerate the split shapes that hit each combination, including the zero-length-update-with-nonzero-leftover no-op and the case where all three run in a single call.","usage":{"total_tokens":64904,"tool_uses":21,"duration_ms":317488},"uuid":"06b7eab9-f120-4def-81ae-83687fe4cda0","session_id":"b566403e-4c11-4a9b-ad3a-d43b1f08afd2"}
