ites `recip` **before** computing its return value, so the out-buffer is fully written even on the `-1` (zero-scalar) path.\n\n**Configuration surface (128 rows)**\n- Covers verify widths x equal/differ-at-byte-k; the three salsa round counts (20/12/8 through the shared static) x `c == NULL` vs non-NULL; hsalsa20/hchacha20 x `c` NULL-ness; keccak `permute_24` (constants 0..23) vs `permute_12` (constants **12..23** — a different window, not a prefix) plus all three `xor_bytes` loop arms; softaes 128/256 key schedules and encrypt/decrypt/last round functions; the full ed25519 and ristretto255 scalar + point APIs with canonical/non-canonical/zero/`L-1` scalar shapes and identity/small-order/cofactor/non-canonical point shapes; and `from_string` x `hash_alg ∈ {1,2}` x `ctx_len ∈ {0, 255, >255}` x `msg_len`.\n\nTwo naming corrections vs. the task brief, noted inline in the artifacts:\n- There is **no `crypto_core_ed25519_from_string_ro`** symbol in 1.0.23. The RO variant is plain `crypto_core_ed25519_from_string` (hashes to 2 points, `h_len = 96`, sums them); `_from_string_nu` is the non-uniform single-point variant (`h_len = 48`).\n- **`crypto_core_ed25519_from_uniform` is not exported.** `ge25519_from_uniform` lives in `private/ed25519_ref10.h` and is reachable publicly only through `crypto_core_ed25519_random`. Likewise `softaes.c` exposes nothing via `sodium.h` — `private/softaes.h` is consumed only by `aegis128l_soft.c`, `aegis256_soft.c`, and `ipcrypt_soft.c`, so its rows are marked as internally-reachable-only.\n\nPer the no-`HAVE_*` build assumption I pinned the fixed paths at the top of both files (`fe_25_5` limbs + `fe_25_5/base.h` tables, `keccak1600_ref_*`, softaes non-`FAVOR_PERFORMANCE` with `SOFTAES_STRIDE == 16`, arithmetic `equal()`/`negative()` fallbacks) so they are not mistaken for configuration axes. `MINIMAL` is also undefined, so `salsa2012`/`salsa208` are present.\n\nNothing outside `translation/phaseA/` was touched; `c_src/` was read-only through