{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_6wvspi54j76cjmgfyurituvtpbddlkpkuuujo7ohhh7qa3mlgcja","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Both artifacts are written.\n\n## Files\n\n- `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-RqaJY6/translation/phaseA/errors_6.md` — **84 rows** (`6.1`–`6.83`, plus one `6.29a` sub-row)\n- `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-RqaJY6/translation/phaseA/configs_6.md` — **129 rows** (`6.1`–`6.129`)\n\n## Key findings\n\n**aes256gcm is entirely dead in this build.** With no `HAVE_*` macros, the `#if !((HAVE_ARMCRYPTO && NATIVE_LITTLE_ENDIAN) || (HAVE_TMMINTRIN_H && HAVE_WMMINTRIN_H))` stub block at `aead_aes256gcm.c:50-157` is what links. `crypto_aead_aes256gcm_is_available()` returns `0`, and all nine other entry points (`_encrypt`, `_encrypt_detached`, `_decrypt`, `_decrypt_detached`, `_beforenm`, `_encrypt_afternm`, `_encrypt_detached_afternm`, `_decrypt_afternm`, `_decrypt_detached_afternm`) unconditionally set `errno = ENOSYS` and return `-1` — **without** writing `*clen_p`/`*mlen_p`/`*maclen_p`, which differs from every other AEAD (they zero the out-length on failure). `_keybytes`/`_nsecbytes`/`_npubbytes`/`_abytes`/`_statebytes`/`_messagebytes_max`/`_keygen` live outside the `#if` and still work.\n\n**Overflow guards are not uniform.** All `mlen > MESSAGEBYTES_MAX` checks call `sodium_misuse()` → `abort()` (never return an error code) — *except* aegis128l/aegis256 `*_decrypt_detached`, which `return -1`. Also, aegis128l/aegis256 `_encrypt_detached` **do** guard `mlen`/`adlen`, whereas the three chacha-family `_encrypt_detached` functions have **no** guards at all and always return `0`.\n\n**Two easy-to-miss ordering details:** aegis `_encrypt_detached` stores `*maclen_p = 32` *before* the overflow check; chacha's stores it *after* the crypto. And `secretstream_pull` writes `*mlen_p = 0`, `*tag_p = 0xff` *before* the `inlen < 17` check.\n\n**Zeroing-on-failure diverges between AEAD and secretbox.** AEAD `_decrypt_detached` does `memset(m, 0, clen)` on tag mismatch (skipped when `m == NULL`); secretbox `_open_detached` leaves `m` completely untouched. secretstream `_pull` also leaves `m` untouched and leaves the state unadvanced.\n\n**Latent hazard in NaCl-style secretbox:** `crypto_secretbox_xsalsa20poly1305` only checks `mlen >= 32`; it never verifies `m[0..31] == 0`. A non-zero padding region returns `0` but produces a permanently unopenable box (errors row 6.63). Also, `crypto_secretbox_xchacha20poly1305` has **no** NaCl-style variant and no `_keygen`.\n\n**secretstream quirks to preserve verbatim:** the tag byte is never validated (any value with bit `0x02` set — including bogus tags — triggers an implicit rekey); `_init_pull` never validates the header; there is no \"stream finished\" latch after `TAG_FINAL`; `_pull` has **no** `m == NULL` verify-only branch (unlike every AEAD) so `m == NULL` with `mlen > 0` is a NULL deref; and the padding expression `(0x10 - (sizeof block) + mlen) & 0xf` is an upstream off-by-`sizeof block` bug (with `slen = 64 + mlen`) that a translation must reproduce exactly."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2304,"cache_read_input_tokens":109254,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2304,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01Au8RFPQHc3481Wbqzfb3cZ","session_id":"b566403e-4c11-4a9b-ad3a-d43b1f08afd2","uuid":"e31834fa-b296-4bfb-80e7-3e0f866cc6a6","timestamp":"2026-08-31T03:42:12.744Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Phase A area 6: aead+secretbox+secretstream"}
