{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_uwz4hlqvnbma563v2qlmvdhcfk2msx5jssdooxy62bqwufkkujaq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_bdrk_019SnHB3DsDmZYZ2StTGaQ75","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Phase B/C tests area 2","subagent_type":"general-purpose","run_in_background":true,"prompt":"Repo root: /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-RqaJY6 (call it $ROOT).\nThis is a C-to-Rust differential verification task for libsodium 1.0.23.\n\nRULES (absolute):\n- `$ROOT/c_src/` is READ-ONLY ground truth. NEVER modify it. The C is ALWAYS correct.\n- The Rust crate is `$ROOT/translation/`. Run all cargo commands from there.\n- Cargo has NO network access. ALWAYS pass `--offline` to cargo.\n- Never call Rust functions directly. Everything goes through `libloading` + `dlsym` on\n  BOTH shared objects. The harness `$ROOT/translation/tests/common/mod.rs` already does this.\n- Use `timeout 600 cargo ...` for every cargo invocation.\n\nREAD FIRST (in this order):\n1. `$ROOT/translation/tests/common/mod.rs` — the shared harness. It exposes:\n   `both::<FnType>(\"symbol\") -> (Symbol<C>, Symbol<Rust>)`, `has(\"symbol\") -> bool`,\n   `eqb(label, &[u8], &[u8])`, `eqi(label, c_int, c_int)`, `hex(&[u8])`,\n   `Rng::new(seed)` (splitmix64: `.next_u64() .next_u32() .byte() .below(n) .range(lo,hi) .bytes(n) .fill(&mut [u8])`),\n   `padded(len)` + `check_pad(label, &v, len)` (out-of-bounds-write detection),\n   `rng_reset()` / `rng_reseed(seed)` (rewinds the deterministic RNG installed into BOTH\n   libraries so C and Rust see identical randomness — call before any pair of calls that\n   consume randomness), `errno()` / `set_errno(v)`, and\n   `eq_abort(label, c_closure, r_closure)` for comparing paths that `abort()` via\n   `sodium_misuse()` (it forks; core dumps are disabled).\n2. `$ROOT/translation/tests/a1_utils.rs` and `$ROOT/translation/tests/a1_codecs.rs` — worked\n   examples of the style expected (property-style loops over many randomized inputs with a\n   fixed seed, out-of-bounds guard checks, errno comparison, abort comparison).\n3. `$ROOT/translation/phaseA/errors_2.md` and `$ROOT/translation/phaseA/configs_2.md` — YOUR\n   WORK LIST. These were derived mechanically from the C source.\n4. The relevant C sources + headers for area 2 (crypto_verify + crypto_core: verify.c,\n   core_salsa_ref.c, core_hsalsa20.c, core_hchacha20.c, keccak1600*.c, softaes.c,\n   core_ed25519.c, core_ristretto255.c, core_h2c.c, ref10/ed25519_ref10.c) — consult them\n   whenever a divergence appears, to decide what the correct behaviour is.\n\nYOUR TASK — Phase B (valid paths) and Phase C (error paths) for AREA 2:\nWrite new test files `$ROOT/translation/tests/a2_verify_core.rs` and, if it gets long, split\ninto `a2_ed25519.rs` / `a2_ristretto255.rs` / `a2_salsa_keccak.rs`. Cover:\n- EVERY row of `configs_2.md`, using MANY randomized inputs per row (fixed seeds), not one\n  hand-picked value. Note that only symbols actually exported can be tested — use `has()` to\n  skip anything not exported by BOTH .so's, and say so in your report.\n- EVERY row of `errors_2.md`, asserting the SAME sentinel value (not merely \"both failed\").\n- Plus the generic FFI boundary cases for this area: zero lengths, one-past-range values,\n  all-zero / all-0xff / non-canonical (>= 2^255-19) field elements, non-canonical scalars,\n  the identity point, all 8 small-order points, and out-of-range `int` enum-ish arguments\n  where any exist.\n\nWhen C and Rust diverge: the C is right. Find the bug in `$ROOT/translation/src/*.rs` and fix\nit there (surgically — other agents are editing other modules concurrently, so touch only\nwhat you must, and never reformat unrelated code). Re-run until green. Report every\ndivergence you found and how you fixed it.\n\nThen EDIT `$ROOT/translation/phaseA/configs_2.md` to change each covered row's `[ ]` to `[x]`,\nand add a trailing `| status |` column value (`verified` / `unreachable-from-public-API` /\n`not-exported`) to each row of `$ROOT/translation/phaseA/errors_2.md`.\n\nFinish by running `timeout 600 cargo test --offline --test a2_verify_core` (and your other new\na2_* test targets) and confirming 0 failures. Report: files created, test count, rows checked\noff, divergences found+fixed, and anything you could NOT cover with the reason."}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":657,"cache_read_input_tokens":159162,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":657,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b566403e-4c11-4a9b-ad3a-d43b1f08afd2","uuid":"1df6a8ee-c539-4bab-b0e8-7ba2e856961f","timestamp":"2026-08-31T03:44:00.173Z"}
