or AREA 2:\nWrite new test files `$ROOT/translation/tests/a2_verify_core.rs` and, if it gets long, split\ninto `a2_ed25519.rs` / `a2_ristretto255.rs` / `a2_salsa_keccak.rs`. Cover:\n- EVERY row of `configs_2.md`, using MANY randomized inputs per row (fixed seeds), not one\n  hand-picked value. Note that only symbols actually exported can be tested — use `has()` to\n  skip anything not exported by BOTH .so's, and say so in your report.\n- EVERY row of `errors_2.md`, asserting the SAME sentinel value (not merely \"both failed\").\n- Plus the generic FFI boundary cases for this area: zero lengths, one-past-range values,\n  all-zero / all-0xff / non-canonical (>= 2^255-19) field elements, non-canonical scalars,\n  the identity point, all 8 small-order points, and out-of-range `int` enum-ish arguments\n  where any exist.\n\nWhen C and Rust diverge: the C is right. Find the bug in `$ROOT/translation/src/*.rs` and fix\nit there (surgically — other agents are editing other modules concurrently, so touch only\nwhat you must, and never reformat unrelated code). Re-run until green. Report every\ndivergence you found and how you fixed it.\n\nThen EDIT `$ROOT/translation/phaseA/configs_2.md` to change each covered row's `[ ]` to `[x]`,\nand add a trailing `| status |` column value (`verified` / `unreachable-from-public-API` /\n`not-exported`) to each row of `$ROOT/translation/phaseA/errors_2.md`.\n\nFinish by running `timeout 600 cargo test --offline --test a2_verify_core` (and your other new\na2_* test targets) and confirming 0 failures. Report: files created, test count, rows checked\noff, divergences found+fixed, and anything you could NOT cover with the reason.","outputFile":"/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-agent-LlK7ZE/tmp/claude-31072124/-local-home-scheschb--harvest-work-harvest-work-RqaJY6/b566403e-4c11-4a9b-ad3a-d43b1f08afd2/tasks/adc1843a77905e6e2.output","canReadOutputFile":true}}
