{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01MoMZL1J36kzkikefPBe5VW","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t## Area 2 — crypto_verify + crypto_core\n2\t\n3\tConfiguration surface = the *valid-input* option/shape combinations that the C code actually branches on (or that select a distinct code path / constant set). Rejection branches live in `errors_2.md`.\n4\t\n5\tBuild assumption: no `HAVE_*` macros are defined by the CMake build, so the following are fixed and are **not** configuration axes:\n6\t\n7\t- `crypto_verify_n` → byte-loop fallback (`verify.c:63`), not the SSE2 `__m128i` variant; `HAVE_INLINE_ASM` optimization barrier absent, so the `optblocker_u16` trick is the only barrier.\n8\t- `ed25519_ref10.c` → `fe_25_5` field arithmetic (`10 x 25.5`-bit limbs) + `fe_25_5/base.h` / `fe_25_5/base2.h` precomputed tables; `equal()` / `negative()` take the arithmetic fallback with `optblocker_u8`.\n9\t- `keccak1600.c` → `keccak1600_ref_*` (no `__ARM_FEATURE_SHA3`).\n10\t- `softaes.c` → the `#else` (non-`FAVOR_PERFORMANCE`) branch, `SOFTAES_STRIDE == 16`, i.e. the on-the-fly 16-entry SBOX slice tables, not `_aes_lut[1024]`.\n11\t- `MINIMAL` is not defined → `crypto_core_salsa2012` and `crypto_core_salsa208` are present.\n12\t\n13\t| # | entry point(s) | configuration (options set + input shape) | [ ] |\n14\t|---|----------------|--------------------------------------------|-----|\n15\t| 2.1 | `crypto_verify_16` | `x == y`, both all-zero 16 bytes | [ ] |\n16\t| 2.2 | `crypto_verify_16` | `x == y`, both random 16 bytes | [ ] |\n17\t| 2.3 | `crypto_verify_16` | differ at byte `k = 0` only, single-bit flip (`x[0] ^ 0x01`) | [ ] |\n18\t| 2.4 | `crypto_verify_16` | differ at byte `k = 15` only (last byte, exercises the full loop before divergence) | [ ] |\n19\t| 2.5 | `crypto_verify_16` | differ at every byte (`y = ~x`) | [ ] |\n20\t| 2.6 | `crypto_verify_32` | `x == y`, 32 bytes (both all-zero and random) | [ ] |\n21\t| 2.7 | `crypto_verify_32`