{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01PuKaGyqy8Sn56H1h1Cp4Ra","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t## Area 3 — hashes / xof / generichash / shorthash\n2\t\n3\tScope: `crypto_hash/{crypto_hash.c, sha256/**, sha512/**, sha3/hash_sha3.c}`,\n4\t`crypto_xof/**` (shake128, shake256, turboshake128, turboshake256 + `ref/`),\n5\t`crypto_generichash/{crypto_generichash.c, blake2b/generichash_blake2.c, blake2b/ref/**}`,\n6\t`crypto_shorthash/**`, and the matching public headers.\n7\t\n8\tBuild assumption: the CMake build defines **no** `HAVE_*` macros, so:\n9\t* `hash_sha256_cp.c` takes the `#else` (portable `SHA256_Transform`) branch — `HAVE_SHA256_ARMCRYPTO` is off.\n10\t* `blake2b-ref.c` uses `blake2b_compress = blake2b_compress_ref` and the `#else` (64-bit pair) branch of\n11\t  `blake2b_increment_counter` (`HAVE_TI_MODE` off).\n12\t* `blake2b_pick_best_implementation()` unconditionally selects `blake2b_compress_ref`.\n13\t\n14\tConstants referenced below: `crypto_hash_sha256_BYTES`=32, `crypto_hash_sha512_BYTES`=64,\n15\t`crypto_hash_sha3256_BYTES`=32, `crypto_hash_sha3512_BYTES`=64, `SHA3_256_RATE`=136, `SHA3_512_RATE`=72,\n16\t`SHAKE128_RATE`=`TURBOSHAKE128_RATE`=168, `SHAKE256_RATE`=`TURBOSHAKE256_RATE`=136,\n17\t`crypto_xof_*_DOMAIN_STANDARD`=0x1F, `SHA3_DOMAIN`=0x06,\n18\t`BLAKE2B_OUTBYTES`=`BLAKE2B_KEYBYTES`=64, `BLAKE2B_BLOCKBYTES`=128, `BLAKE2B_SALTBYTES`=`BLAKE2B_PERSONALBYTES`=16,\n19\t`crypto_generichash_blake2b_BYTES_MIN`=16, `_BYTES`=32, `_BYTES_MAX`=64,\n20\t`_KEYBYTES_MIN`=16, `_KEYBYTES`=32, `_KEYBYTES_MAX`=64,\n21\t`crypto_shorthash_siphash24_BYTES`=8/`KEYBYTES`=16, `crypto_shorthash_siphashx24_BYTES`=16/`KEYBYTES`=16.\n22\t\n23\t`sodium_misuse()` (sodium/core.c:192) calls the registered misuse handler if any and then `abort()` — i.e. it\n24\tnever returns. Rows marked \"abort\" are process-terminating, not `-1`-returning.\n25\t\n26\t| # | function | trigger (exact invalid input/condition) | expected C result |\n27\