{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_015mH599oJ2qgATyQnhDBupa","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t## Area 4 — crypto_auth + crypto_onetimeauth\n2\t\n3\tConfiguration axes taken directly from the source:\n4\t\n5\t- **Primitive**: `hmacsha256` (SHA-256, block 64, tag 32, `crypto_verify_32`), `hmacsha512` (SHA-512, block 128, tag 64, `crypto_verify_64`), `hmacsha512256` (SHA-512 internally, tag truncated to 32, `crypto_verify_32`), `poly1305` (block 16, tag 16, `crypto_verify_16`).\n6\t- **Entry style**: one-shot `*_auth(out, in, inlen, k)` vs. streaming `*_init` / `*_update` / `*_final`. The one-shot HMAC functions are literally `init(&state, k, KEYBYTES); update(...); final(...)`, so streaming with a 32-byte key must be bit-identical.\n7\t- **Key length** (HMAC only — `*_init` takes an explicit `keylen`): `keylen < BLOCKBYTES`, `keylen == BLOCKBYTES` (must **not** hash), `keylen > BLOCKBYTES` (hashed to 32 / 64 bytes). `poly1305` has no keylen parameter — always exactly 32 bytes.\n8\t- **Message length / update splitting**: pad and block boundaries of the underlying hash, plus multi-`update` splits that straddle those boundaries and the poly1305 16-byte `leftover` buffer.\n9\t- **Wrapper level**: generic `crypto_auth*` / `crypto_onetimeauth*` vs. primitive-specific entry points, plus the `*bytes` / `*keybytes` / `*statebytes` / `*primitive` accessors.\n10\t- **Build config**: no `HAVE_*` macros are defined, so poly1305 uses `donna` with `poly1305_donna32.h` (32-bit limbs); `sse2/` is not compiled, `crypto_verify_n` and `sodium_memcmp` take their portable branches.\n11\t\n12\t### CONFIGURATION SURFACE\n13\t\n14\t| # | entry point(s) | configuration (options set + input shape) | [ ] |\n15\t|---|----------------|--------------------------------------------|-----|\n16\t| 4.1 | `crypto_auth` | generic one-shot wrapper; 32-byte key; must be byte-identical to `crypto_auth_hmacsha512256` for every message length in {0,1,55,56,63,64,65,111,112,127,128,129} | [ ] |\n17\t| 4.2 | `crypto_auth_verify` | generic verify; good 32-byte tag ⇒ `0`; tag with one flipped bit ⇒ `-1`; identical results to `crypto_auth_hmacsha512256_verify` | [ ] |\n18\t| 4.3 | `crypto_auth_keygen` | fills exactly `crypto_auth_KEYBYTES` = 32 bytes from `randombytes_buf`; two successive calls differ; no bytes written past index 31 | [ ] |\n19\t| 4.4 | `crypto_auth_primitive` | returns the literal `\"hmacsha512256\"` (`crypto_auth_PRIMITIVE`) | [ ] |\n20\t| 4.5 | `crypto_auth_bytes` / `crypto_auth_keybytes` | return 32 / 32, matching the macros `crypto_auth_BYTES` = `crypto_auth_hmacsha512256_BYTES` and `crypto_auth_KEYBYTES` = `crypto_auth_hmacsha512256_KEYBYTES` | [ ] |\n21\t| 4.6 | `crypto_auth.h` surface shape | the generic `crypto_auth` API deliberately exposes **no** state type, **no** `crypto_auth_statebytes`, and **no** init/update/final — streaming is only reachable through the primitive-specific names. Port must not invent a generic streaming API | [ ] |\n22\t| 4.7 | `crypto_auth_hmacsha256` | one-shot; 32-byte key; `inlen = 0` (empty message) | [ ] |\n23\t| 4.8 | `crypto_auth_hmacsha256` | one-shot; 32-byte key; `inlen = 1` | [ ] |\n24\t| 4.9 | `crypto_auth_hmacsha256` | one-shot; 32-byte key; `inlen = 55` (inner hash: last block has exactly 9 bytes for pad+length after the 64-byte ipad block) | [ ] |\n25\t| 4.10 | `crypto_auth_hmacsha256` | one-shot; 32-byte key; `inlen = 56` (pad spills into an extra SHA-256 block) | [ ] |\n26\t| 4.11 | `crypto_auth_hmacsha256` | one-shot; 32-byte key; `inlen = 63` | [ ] |\n27\t| 4.12 | `crypto_auth_hmacsha256` | one-shot; 32-byte key; `inlen = 64` (exactly one SHA-256 block after the ipad block) | [ ] |\n28\t| 4.13 | `crypto_auth_hmacsha256` | one-shot; 32-byte key; `inlen = 65` | [ ] |\n29\t| 4.14 | `crypto_auth_hmacsha256` | one-shot; 32-byte key; `inlen = 111` | [ ] |\n30\t| 4.15 | `crypto_auth_hmacsha256` | one-shot; 32-byte key; `inlen = 112` | [ ] |\n31\t| 4.16 | `crypto_auth_hmacsha256` | one-shot; 32-byte key; `inlen = 127` | [ ] |\n32\t| 4.17 | `crypto_auth_hmacsha256` | one-shot; 32-byte key; `inlen = 128` (two full blocks) | [ ] |\n33\t| 4.18 | `crypto_auth_hmacsha256` | one-shot; 32-byte key; `inlen = 129` | [ ] |\n34\t| 4.19 | `crypto_auth_hmacsha256_init` + `_update` + `_final` | streaming, `keylen = 32`, single `update`, `inlen = 0`; must equal 4.7 | [ ] |\n35\t| 4.20 | `crypto_auth_hmacsha256_init/_update/_final` | streaming, `keylen = 32`, single `update`, `inlen = 1`; must equal 4.8 | [ ] |\n36\t| 4.21 | `crypto_auth_hmacsha256_init/_update/_final` | streaming, `keylen = 32`, single `update`, `inlen = 55`; must equal 4.9 | [ ] |\n37\t| 4.22 | `crypto_auth_hmacsha256_init/_update/_final` | streaming, `keylen = 32`, single `update`, `inlen = 56`; must equal 4.10 | [ ] |\n38\t| 4.23 | `crypto_auth_hmacsha256_init/_update/_final` | streaming, `keylen = 32`, single `update`, `inlen = 63`; must equal 4.11 | [ ] |\n39\t| 4.24 | `crypto_auth_hmacsha256_init/_update/_final` | streaming, `keylen = 32`, single `update`, `inlen = 64`; must equal 4.12 | [ ] |\n40\t| 4.25 | `crypto_auth_hmacsha256_init/_update/_final` | streaming, `keylen = 32`, single `update`, `inlen = 65`; must equal 4.13 | [ ] |\n41\t| 4.26 | `crypto_auth_hmacsha256_init/_update/_final` | streaming, `keylen = 32`, single `update`, `inlen = 111`; must equal 4.14 | [ ] |\n42\t| 4.27 | `crypto_auth_hmacsha256_init/_update/_final` | streaming, `keylen = 32`, single `update`, `inlen = 112`; must equal 4.15 | [ ] |\n43\t| 4.28 | `crypto_auth_hmacsha256_init/_update/_final` | streaming, `keylen = 32`, single `update`, `inlen = 127`; must equal 4.16 | [ ] |\n44\t| 4.29 | `crypto_auth_hmacsha256_init/_update/_final` | streaming, `keylen = 32`, single `update`, `inlen = 128`; must equal 4.17 | [ ] |\n45\t| 4.30 | `crypto_auth_hmacsha256_init/_update/_final` | streaming, `keylen = 32`, single `update`, `inlen = 129`; must equal 4.18 | [ ] |\n46\t| 4.31 | `crypto_auth_hmacsha256_u