e style expected.\n3. `$ROOT/translation/phaseA/errors_5.md` and `$ROOT/translation/phaseA/configs_5.md` — YOUR\n   WORK LIST (89 config rows, 29 error rows). Derived mechanically from the C source.\n4. The relevant C sources + headers for area 5 (crypto_stream/: crypto_stream.c,\n   chacha20/stream_chacha20.c + ref/chacha20_ref.c, salsa20/ + ref/, salsa2012/, salsa208/,\n   xsalsa20/, xchacha20/) — consult them on any divergence.\n\nYOUR TASK — Phase B (valid paths) and Phase C (error paths) for AREA 5:\nWrite new test files under `$ROOT/translation/tests/`, e.g. `a5_stream.rs` (split into\n`a5_chacha20.rs` / `a5_salsa.rs` if it gets long). Cover:\n- EVERY row of `configs_5.md`, with MANY randomized inputs per row (fixed seeds). For each\n  primitive, exercise the keystream form, the `_xor` form and the `_xor_ic` form; assert the\n  keystream form equals `_xor` against a zero plaintext; assert `_xor` is an involution;\n  assert `_xor_ic(ic=k)` equals the tail of a long `_xor` starting at block k. Sweep message\n  lengths 0..600 plus a few multi-KiB values, and initial counters 0, 1, small values, and\n  values chosen so the 64-bit / 32-bit block counter rolls over mid-message (use\n  `crypto_stream_chacha20_ietf_ext_xor_ic` to reach the counter-overflow-into-nonce path with\n  a small message).\n- EVERY row of `errors_5.md`, asserting the SAME outcome. Note that area 5 has NO `return -1`\n  paths — the only failure mechanism is `sodium_misuse()` → `abort()`, so most error rows need\n  `eq_abort`. Be careful: allocating a 2^38-byte buffer is impossible; for the length-limit\n  rows pass a length that exceeds the limit together with a pointer that the C never\n  dereferences before the check (verify by reading the C), or use a much smaller mapping and\n  document the row as `checked-via-guard-only`. Do NOT skip the reachable IETF\n  `MESSAGEBYTES_MAX` and 32-bit-counter rows.\n- Additionally, verify the accessor functions (`*_keybytes`, `*_noncebytes`,\n  `*_messagebytes_max`, `crypto_stream_primitive`, `crypto_stream_keybytes` ...) and\n  `*_keygen` (with `rng_reset()` before each pair).\n\nWhen C and Rust diverge: the C is right. Find the bug in `$ROOT/translation/src/*.rs` and fix\nit there (surgically — other agents are editing other modules concurrently, so touch only\nwhat you must, and never reformat unrelated code). Re-run until green.\n\nThen EDIT `$ROOT/translation/phaseA/configs_5.md` to change each covered row's `[ ]` to `[x]`,\nand add a trailing status value (`verified` / `dead-branch-on-this-build` /\n`checked-via-guard-only`) to each row of `$ROOT/translation/phaseA/errors_5.md`.\n\nFinish by running your new test targets with `timeout 600 cargo test --offline --test <name>`\nand confirming 0 failures. Report: files created, test count, rows checked off, divergences\nfound+fixed, and anything you could NOT cover with the reason."}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9873,"cache_read_input_tokens":159819,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":9873,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":17,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b566403e-4c11-4a9b-ad3a-d43b1f08afd2","uuid":"c9952c2c-02fc-4a53-8013-33df3fcd3b99","timestamp":"2026-08-31T03:45:17.215Z"}
