{"type":"system","subtype":"task_notification","task_id":"afc550a4aecdcc2c0","tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01CowTwzXeKcb75YMkUZC5tB","status":"completed","output_file":"/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-agent-LlK7ZE/tmp/claude-31072124/-local-home-scheschb--harvest-work-harvest-work-RqaJY6/b566403e-4c11-4a9b-ad3a-d43b1f08afd2/tasks/afc550a4aecdcc2c0.output","summary":"Both artifacts are written.\n\n## Files\n\n- `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-RqaJY6/translation/phaseA/errors_7.md` — **129 rows** (`7.1`–`7.129`), contiguous, no duplicates\n- `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-RqaJY6/translation/phaseA/configs_7.md` — **130 rows** (`7.1`–`7.130`), contiguous, no duplicates\n\nBoth follow the existing `errors_5.md` house style: file list, a resolved-constants table (LP64, no `HAVE_*`), a \"global observations\" section, then the numbered table.\n\n## Key findings worth flagging to the porter\n\n- **`crypto_scalarmult_curve25519_base` bypasses the wrapper.** It calls `...ref10_implementation.mult_base` directly (`scalarmult_curve25519.c:33-35`), so the all-zero-output guard `-(1 & ((d - 1) >> 8))` applies **only** to the 2-argument form. `_base` can never fail — not even for `n = 0`.\n- **Output-buffer aliasing on failure is load-bearing.** All ed25519/ristretto255 scalarmult functions stage the clamped scalar in the caller's `q` (`unsigned char *t = q;`). Early rejects (`ge25519_is_canonical`, `ristretto255_frombytes`, `has_small_order(p)`) leave `q` untouched; late rejects (`_is_inf(q)`, `sodium_is_zero`) leave `q` fully written. Rows 7.13–7.33 mark which is which.\n- **ed25519 verification is cofactored**: `return ge25519_has_small_order(&check) - 1;` — success requires `check` to be *small-order*, not the identity.\n- **Two real asymmetries in pk validation.** `verify_detached` checks `ge25519_is_canonical(pk)` but *not* `is_on_main_subgroup`; `pk_to_curve25519` checks `is_on_main_subgroup` but *not* canonicality. Rows 7.44 / 7.55 / 7.56.\n- **`crypto_kx` aliasing footgun** (rows 7.94–7.97): with `tx == NULL`, the client's byte-interleaved loop (`rx[i]=keys[i]; tx[i]=keys[i+32]`) leaves the caller's `rx` buffer holding the **tx** key. Server has the reverse loop order. Must be replicated exactly.\n- **mlkem768 `_dec` never returns `-1`** — implicit rejection via `cmov` of `SHAKE256(z ‖ ct)`, no ciphertext validation at all. This makes the `mlkem768_dec != 0` branch in `crypto_kem_xwing_dec` dead; the *only* reachable xwing decapsulation failure is a small-order `ct[1088..1119]` (row 7.121), which is inside an `LCOV_EXCL` region and therefore untested upstream.\n- **Seed-length contract mismatch** (row 7.126): `crypto_kem_xwing_SEEDBYTES == 32` for `_seed_keypair`, but `_enc_deterministic` takes `seed[64]`; mlkem768 is the mirror image (64 vs 32). Unchecked at runtime — worth distinct fixed-size types in Rust.\n- **`sodium_misuse()` (abort, not `-1`)** occurs at 7 sites: the 3 xsalsa/generic box easy+seal `mlen` guards, the 3 xchacha equivalents, and kx with both `rx` and `tx` NULL.\n- xchacha20poly1305 provides **no** NaCl-padded `crypto_box...()`/`_open()`/`_afternm()` and no `_zerobytes`/`_boxzerobytes` (row 7.79) — a port must not invent them.","usage":{"total_tokens":151581,"tool_uses":26,"duration_ms":616556},"uuid":"595d54b1-74de-4de1-ac7c-efa96da46421","session_id":"b566403e-4c11-4a9b-ad3a-d43b1f08afd2"}
