e style expected.\n3. `$ROOT/translation/phaseA/errors_6.md` and `$ROOT/translation/phaseA/configs_6.md` — YOUR\n   WORK LIST (129 config rows, 84 error rows). Derived mechanically from the C source.\n4. The relevant C sources + headers for area 6 (crypto_aead/: aegis128l, aegis256, aes256gcm,\n   chacha20poly1305, xchacha20poly1305; crypto_secretbox/; crypto_secretstream/) — consult\n   them on any divergence.\n\nYOUR TASK — Phase B (valid paths) and Phase C (error paths) for AREA 6:\nWrite new test files under `$ROOT/translation/tests/`, e.g. `a6_aead.rs`, `a6_secretbox.rs`,\n`a6_secretstream.rs`. Cover:\n- EVERY row of `configs_6.md`, with MANY randomized inputs per row (fixed seeds). For each\n  AEAD: combined and detached encrypt/decrypt, ad NULL / empty / random lengths, message\n  lengths sweeping 0..300 plus a few multi-KiB, out-length pointers NULL and non-NULL, and a\n  full encrypt-then-decrypt round trip plus a cross-check that the C ciphertext decrypts under\n  Rust and vice versa. For aes256gcm ALSO cover `_beforenm` + all four `*_afternm` variants\n  and `_is_available` (in this build the whole family is the ENOSYS stub — verify the exact\n  `-1` + `errno` and that `*clen_p`/`*mlen_p`/`*maclen_p` are left UNWRITTEN, which differs\n  from the other AEADs). For secretbox cover `_easy`/`_open_easy`, `_detached`/\n  `_open_detached`, the NaCl-style zero-padded `crypto_secretbox`/`_open`, and both primitive\n  families. For secretstream drive full multi-message push/pull sessions with randomized tag\n  sequences (MESSAGE / PUSH / REKEY / FINAL), explicit `_rekey` calls, and compare the FULL\n  opaque state struct bytes between C and Rust after every operation (size it with\n  `crypto_secretstream_xchacha20poly1305_statebytes()`).\n- EVERY row of `errors_6.md`, asserting the SAME sentinel value and, where the C sets it, the\n  same `errno`. Use `eq_abort` for the `sodium_misuse()` overflow rows. Also assert the\n  documented zero-on-failure behaviour differences (AEAD `_decrypt_detached` memsets `m`;\n  secretbox `_open_detached` and secretstream `_pull` do NOT).\n- Plus generic FFI boundary cases: ciphertext exactly ABYTES-1 / ABYTES / ABYTES+1, tag\n  corrupted in every byte position, nonce/key all-zero and all-0xff, `nsec` non-NULL, and\n  out-of-range tag byte values (0x00..0xff) into `_push`.\n\nWhen C and Rust diverge: the C is right. Find the bug in `$ROOT/translation/src/*.rs` and fix\nit there (surgically — other agents are editing other modules concurrently, so touch only\nwhat you must, and never reformat unrelated code). Re-run until green.\n\nThen EDIT `$ROOT/translation/phaseA/configs_6.md` to change each covered row's `[ ]` to `[x]`,\nand add a trailing status value (`verified` / `unreachable-from-public-API` /\n`undefined-behaviour-not-tested`) to each row of `$ROOT/translation/phaseA/errors_6.md`.\n\nFinish by running your new test targets with `timeout 600 cargo test --offline --test <name>`\nand confirming 0 failures. Report: files created, test count, rows checked off, divergences\nfound+fixed, and anything you could NOT cover with the reason."}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9873,"cache_read_input_tokens":159819,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":9873,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":17,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b566403e-4c11-4a9b-ad3a-d43b1f08afd2","uuid":"0deb4fed-b9cb-4db2-9aac-28c571d69b58","timestamp":"2026-08-31T03:45:37.010Z"}
