_pull` do NOT).\n- Plus generic FFI boundary cases: ciphertext exactly ABYTES-1 / ABYTES / ABYTES+1, tag\n  corrupted in every byte position, nonce/key all-zero and all-0xff, `nsec` non-NULL, and\n  out-of-range tag byte values (0x00..0xff) into `_push`.\n\nWhen C and Rust diverge: the C is right. Find the bug in `$ROOT/translation/src/*.rs` and fix\nit there (surgically — other agents are editing other modules concurrently, so touch only\nwhat you must, and never reformat unrelated code). Re-run until green.\n\nThen EDIT `$ROOT/translation/phaseA/configs_6.md` to change each covered row's `[ ]` to `[x]`,\nand add a trailing status value (`verified` / `unreachable-from-public-API` /\n`undefined-behaviour-not-tested`) to each row of `$ROOT/translation/phaseA/errors_6.md`.\n\nFinish by running your new test targets with `timeout 600 cargo test --offline --test <name>`\nand confirming 0 failures. Report: files created, test count, rows checked off, divergences\nfound+fixed, and anything you could NOT cover with the reason.","uuid":"4926f234-d012-4978-855b-1bddf3e7a402","session_id":"b566403e-4c11-4a9b-ad3a-d43b1f08afd2"}
