{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_u7jdzdamvi6xpii66btiotvq3culbb6gl3kg5x36o3oaj77calfq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_bdrk_01PC38MgRfdqoE1HMCuVcz7v","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Phase B/C tests area 7","subagent_type":"general-purpose","run_in_background":true,"prompt":"Repo root: /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-RqaJY6 (call it $ROOT).\nThis is a C-to-Rust differential verification task for libsodium 1.0.23.\n\nRULES (absolute):\n- `$ROOT/c_src/` is READ-ONLY ground truth. NEVER modify it. The C is ALWAYS correct.\n- The Rust crate is `$ROOT/translation/`. Run all cargo commands from there.\n- Cargo has NO network access. ALWAYS pass `--offline` to cargo.\n- Never call Rust functions directly. Everything goes through `libloading` + `dlsym` on\n  BOTH shared objects. The harness `$ROOT/translation/tests/common/mod.rs` already does this.\n- Use `timeout 600 cargo ...` for every cargo invocation.\n\nREAD FIRST (in this order):\n1. `$ROOT/translation/tests/common/mod.rs` — the shared harness. It exposes:\n   `both::<FnType>(\"symbol\") -> (Symbol<C>, Symbol<Rust>)`, `has(\"symbol\") -> bool`,\n   `eqb(label, &[u8], &[u8])`, `eqi(label, c_int, c_int)`, `hex(&[u8])`,\n   `Rng::new(seed)` (splitmix64: `.next_u64() .next_u32() .byte() .below(n) .range(lo,hi) .bytes(n) .fill(&mut [u8])`),\n   `padded(len)` + `check_pad(label, &v, len)` (out-of-bounds-write detection),\n   `rng_reset()` / `rng_reseed(seed)` (rewinds the deterministic RNG installed into BOTH\n   libraries so C and Rust see identical randomness — call before any pair of calls that\n   consume randomness, e.g. `*_keypair`, `*_seal`, `*_enc`), `errno()` / `set_errno(v)`, and\n   `eq_abort(label, c_closure, r_closure)` for comparing paths that `abort()` via\n   `sodium_misuse()` (it forks; core dumps are disabled).\n2. `$ROOT/translation/tests/a1_utils.rs` and `$ROOT/translation/tests/a1_codecs.rs` — worked\n   examples of the style expected.\n3. `$ROOT/translation/phaseA/errors_7.md` and `$ROOT/translation/phaseA/configs_7.md` — YOUR\n   WORK LIST (~130 rows each). Derived mechanically from the C source. Read the\n   \"global observations\" section carefully — it lists the subtle behaviours to assert.\n4. The relevant C sources + headers for area 7 (crypto_scalarmult/, crypto_sign/,\n   crypto_box/, crypto_kx/, crypto_kdf/, crypto_kem/) — consult them on any divergence.\n\nYOUR TASK — Phase B (valid paths) and Phase C (error paths) for AREA 7:\nWrite new test files under `$ROOT/translation/tests/`: `a7_scalarmult.rs`, `a7_sign.rs`,\n`a7_box.rs`, `a7_kx_kdf.rs`, `a7_kem.rs`. Cover:\n- EVERY row of `configs_7.md`, with MANY randomized inputs per row (fixed seeds). Include\n  full round trips, cross-library round trips (C output consumed by Rust and vice versa), the\n  multipart sign API with randomized chunk splits, and the `_beforenm`/`*_afternm` box state\n  API. For anything that consumes randomness call `rng_reset()` before the C call and rely on\n  the harness's per-library independent identical streams.\n- EVERY row of `errors_7.md`, asserting the SAME sentinel value. Critically, ALSO assert the\n  documented output-buffer-on-failure behaviour the artifact calls out (early rejects leave\n  `q` untouched, late rejects leave it fully written) by pre-filling the output buffer with a\n  known pattern and comparing C vs Rust byte for byte after a failure.\n- Plus generic FFI boundary cases: all-zero and all-0xff scalars/points/keys, non-canonical\n  field elements (>= 2^255-19), the identity point, all 8 small-order curve25519 points and\n  the corresponding ed25519 ones, non-reduced scalars, signatures with non-canonical S,\n  `subkey_len` of 0 / MIN-1 / MIN / MAX / MAX+1 for kdf, `out_len` past the HKDF limit,\n  ciphertexts one byte short/long for kem, and NULL `rx`/`tx` for kx.\n\nWhen C and Rust diverge: the C is right. Find the bug in `$ROOT/translation/src/*.rs` and fix\nit there (surgically — other agents are editing other modules concurrently, so touch only\nwhat you must, and never reformat unrelated code). Re-run until green.\n\nThen EDIT `$ROOT/translation/phaseA/configs_7.md` to change each covered row's `[ ]` to `[x]`,\nand add a trailing status value (`verified` / `unreachable-from-public-API` /\n`undefined-behaviour-not-tested`) to each row of `$ROOT/translation/phaseA/errors_7.md`.\n\nFinish by running your new test targets with `timeout 600 cargo test --offline --test <name>`\nand confirming 0 failures. Report: files created, test count, rows checked off, divergences\nfound+fixed, and anything you could NOT cover with the reason."}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9006,"cache_read_input_tokens":169692,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":9006,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":17,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b566403e-4c11-4a9b-ad3a-d43b1f08afd2","uuid":"d2a75f26-232e-4c12-8354-c61e36b7f44b","timestamp":"2026-08-31T03:46:02.491Z"}
