{"type":"system","subtype":"task_notification","task_id":"ae098cdf98b9d7976","tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01E1kRBgn7dnZU4dv3hDQ4tS","status":"completed","output_file":"/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-agent-LlK7ZE/tmp/claude-31072124/-local-home-scheschb--harvest-work-harvest-work-RqaJY6/b566403e-4c11-4a9b-ad3a-d43b1f08afd2/tasks/ae098cdf98b9d7976.output","summary":"Both artifacts are complete and internally consistent.\n\n## Files written\n\n- `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-RqaJY6/translation/phaseA/errors_8.md` — **214 rows** (`8.1` … `8.214`)\n- `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-RqaJY6/translation/phaseA/configs_8.md` — **150 rows** (`8.1` … `8.150`)\n\nNothing outside `translation/phaseA/` was touched; `c_src/` was read-only.\n\n## Key findings worth flagging to the caller\n\n1. **`crypto_pwhash_str_alg` aborts rather than returning `-1`** for an unknown `alg` — it falls through to `sodium_misuse()`. This is the only abort in the argon2 path (`escrypt_PBKDF2_SHA256` with `dkLen > 0x1fffffffe0` is the only one in the scrypt path). A Rust port that returns `-1` here would be observably wrong.\n2. **Large families of `argon2_error_codes` are unreachable on a 64-bit build.** `OUTPUT_TOO_LONG`, `PWD_TOO_LONG`, `SALT_TOO_LONG`, `AD_TOO_*`, `SECRET_TOO_*`, `TIME_TOO_LARGE`, `MEMORY_TOO_MUCH` are all dead through `argon2_context` (the fields are `uint32_t` and the maxima are `UINT32_MAX`); `PWD_TOO_LONG`/`OUTPUT_TOO_LONG`/`SALT_TOO_LONG` are reachable only via `argon2_hash`'s `size_t` parameters. `FREE_MEMORY_CBK_NULL` (-23), `ALLOCATE_MEMORY_CBK_NULL` (-24), `OUT_PTR_MISMATCH` (-27), `MISSING_ARGS` (-30), `THREAD_FAIL` (-33) are never produced anywhere in this fork.\n3. **Version mismatch returns `ARGON2_INCORRECT_TYPE` (-26), not `DECODING_FAIL`** — `argon2_decode_string` uses -26 for `v != 19`, and also for the three dead `> UINT32_MAX` guards.\n4. **Scrypt enforces no `opslimit`/`memlimit` minimum.** `crypto_pwhash_scryptsalsa208sha256(…, opslimit = 0, memlimit = 0)` *succeeds* (`pickparams` clamps `opslimit` to 32768 and yields `N=2, r=8, p=512`), which is asymmetric with the argon2 entry points that return `-1`/`EINVAL`. `pickparams` can never fail, so several `-1`/`EINVAL` branches in the scrypt wrappers are dead.\n5. **`crypto_pwhash_str_needs_rehash` compares only `t_cost` and `m_cost`** — not `p`/`lanes` and not the argon2 type — and divides `memlimit` by 1024 with truncation. Both are behavioural quirks that must be replicated.\n6. **Output buffers are mutated before validation** in every wrapper (`memset(out, 0, outlen)` in `crypto_pwhash_argon2*`, `randombytes_buf(hash, hashlen)` in `argon2_hash`, `randombytes_buf(buf, buflen)` in `escrypt_r`), so a rejected call still clobbers caller memory.\n7. **`argon2_finalize` ignores `blake2b_long`'s return value** — a hypothetical hash failure would leave `context->out` untouched while `argon2_ctx` still returns `ARGON2_OK`.\n8. **`crypto_ipcrypt` is totally error-free**: every public function is `void` with no validation and no authentication tag, so its \"error surface\" is empty. The only data-dependent branches are the degenerate-key fixups in NDX/PFX (`k[0..16) == k[16..32)` → data key becomes `k[i] ^ 0x5a`) and `is_ipv4_mapped` in PFX.\n9. **libsodium 1.0.23 has no `crypto_ipcrypt_*_str` entry points.** The IP-string ↔ 16-byte conversions the task description referred to are `sodium_ip2bin` / `sodium_bin2ip` in `sodium/codecs.c`, which is outside area 8's file list. I recorded their rejection set as rows 8.213/8.214 (errors) and 8.150 (configs), explicitly marked as belonging to the utils/codecs area so ownership stays unambiguous.","usage":{"total_tokens":193595,"tool_uses":36,"duration_ms":692653},"uuid":"227da3ba-137c-4cae-bc41-d9ac8dccae8a","session_id":"b566403e-4c11-4a9b-ad3a-d43b1f08afd2"}
