{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_3d6mxw227pn4zzw7pnqkxqa3ul7bxo43isyxwcosrxaonc7z5opa","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_bdrk_013PupbdJbvdcm1hFvbZnzS8","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Phase B/C tests area 8","subagent_type":"general-purpose","run_in_background":true,"prompt":"Repo root: /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-RqaJY6 (call it $ROOT).\nThis is a C-to-Rust differential verification task for libsodium 1.0.23.\n\nRULES (absolute):\n- `$ROOT/c_src/` is READ-ONLY ground truth. NEVER modify it. The C is ALWAYS correct.\n- The Rust crate is `$ROOT/translation/`. Run all cargo commands from there.\n- Cargo has NO network access. ALWAYS pass `--offline` to cargo.\n- Never call Rust functions directly. Everything goes through `libloading` + `dlsym` on\n  BOTH shared objects. The harness `$ROOT/translation/tests/common/mod.rs` already does this.\n- Use `timeout 600 cargo ...` for every cargo invocation. pwhash is SLOW — keep every\n  argon2/scrypt parameter set at or near the documented minimum so the suite stays fast, and\n  say so in the test comments.\n\nREAD FIRST (in this order):\n1. `$ROOT/translation/tests/common/mod.rs` — the shared harness. It exposes:\n   `both::<FnType>(\"symbol\") -> (Symbol<C>, Symbol<Rust>)`, `has(\"symbol\") -> bool`,\n   `eqb(label, &[u8], &[u8])`, `eqi(label, c_int, c_int)`, `hex(&[u8])`,\n   `Rng::new(seed)` (splitmix64: `.next_u64() .next_u32() .byte() .below(n) .range(lo,hi) .bytes(n) .fill(&mut [u8])`),\n   `padded(len)` + `check_pad(label, &v, len)` (out-of-bounds-write detection),\n   `rng_reset()` / `rng_reseed(seed)` (rewinds the deterministic RNG installed into BOTH\n   libraries so C and Rust see identical randomness — call before any pair of calls that\n   consume randomness, e.g. `crypto_pwhash_str`, which generates a random salt),\n   `errno()` / `set_errno(v)`, and `eq_abort(label, c_closure, r_closure)` for comparing paths\n   that `abort()` via `sodium_misuse()` (it forks; core dumps are disabled).\n2. `$ROOT/translation/tests/a1_utils.rs` and `$ROOT/translation/tests/a1_codecs.rs` — worked\n   examples of the style expected.\n3. `$ROOT/translation/phaseA/errors_8.md` (214 rows!) and\n   `$ROOT/translation/phaseA/configs_8.md` — YOUR WORK LIST, derived mechanically from the C.\n4. The relevant C sources + headers for area 8 (crypto_pwhash/crypto_pwhash.c,\n   crypto_pwhash/argon2/*, crypto_pwhash/scryptsalsa208sha256/*, crypto_ipcrypt/*) — consult\n   them on any divergence.\n\nYOUR TASK — Phase B (valid paths) and Phase C (error paths) for AREA 8:\nWrite new test files under `$ROOT/translation/tests/`: `a8_argon2.rs`, `a8_scrypt.rs`,\n`a8_ipcrypt.rs` (split further if useful). Cover:\n- EVERY row of `configs_8.md`, with several randomized inputs per row (fixed seeds). Include\n  the LOW-LEVEL entry points (`argon2_ctx`, `argon2_hash`, `argon2i_hash_raw`,\n  `argon2id_hash_raw`, `argon2*_hash_encoded`, `argon2_verify`, `argon2_encodedlen`,\n  `encode_string`/`decode_string` if exported, `crypto_pwhash_scryptsalsa208sha256_ll`,\n  `escrypt_*`), not just the `crypto_pwhash*` convenience wrappers. Use `has()` to skip\n  anything not exported by BOTH .so's and report what you skipped.\n- EVERY row of `errors_8.md`, asserting the EXACT numeric error code (the argon2 error enum\n  values are distinct negative integers — assert the specific value, never just \"non-zero\").\n  Also differentially compare `argon2_error_message()` strings if that symbol is exported.\n- Round-trip the encoded strings: `crypto_pwhash_str` / `_str_alg` then `_str_verify` and\n  `_str_needs_rehash` across both libraries in BOTH directions (C-produced string verified by\n  Rust and vice versa), and the same for the scrypt `$7$` format.\n- Plus generic FFI boundary cases: `alg` values with no valid variant (0, 3, 4, -1, INT_MAX,\n  INT_MIN) passed across the FFI boundary, opslimit/memlimit one step below MIN and one step\n  above MAX, `outlen` 0 / MIN-1 / MIN, zero-length password and salt, salt one byte short,\n  truncated and garbage-prefixed encoded strings, and every malformed `$argon2i$` /\n  `$argon2id$` / `$7$` string shape the decoder distinguishes.\n\nWhen C and Rust diverge: the C is right. Find the bug in `$ROOT/translation/src/*.rs` and fix\nit there (surgically — other agents are editing other modules concurrently, so touch only\nwhat you must, and never reformat unrelated code). Re-run until green.\n\nThen EDIT `$ROOT/translation/phaseA/configs_8.md` to change each covered row's `[ ]` to `[x]`,\nand add a trailing status value (`verified` / `unreachable-from-public-API` / `not-exported`)\nto each row of `$ROOT/translation/phaseA/errors_8.md`.\n\nFinish by running your new test targets with `timeout 600 cargo test --offline --test <name>`\nand confirming 0 failures. Report: files created, test count, rows checked off, divergences\nfound+fixed, and anything you could NOT cover with the reason."}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":544,"cache_read_input_tokens":203529,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":544,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b566403e-4c11-4a9b-ad3a-d43b1f08afd2","uuid":"7fce7bc7-b6b8-4ff2-a1d1-d23899cde597","timestamp":"2026-08-31T03:47:36.321Z"}
