{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01SbM16EF2Fh5btCd69o6rNE","type":"tool_result","content":"## Area 1 — sodium core + randombytes\n\nConfiguration surface: valid-input combinations that the compiled C actually branches on.\nSame build assumptions as `errors_1.md` (x86-64 Linux, no `HAVE_*`, `-std=c99`, asserts live, `HAVE_LINUX_COMPATIBLE_GETRANDOM` and `BLOCK_ON_DEV_RANDOM` active, `page_size == DEFAULT_PAGE_SIZE == 0x10000`, `CANARY_SIZE == 16`, `GARBAGE_VALUE == 0xdb`, `TLS` empty).\n\n### version.h / runtime.h / core.h\n\n| # | entry point(s) | configuration (options set + input shape) | [ ] |\n|---|----------------|--------------------------------------------|-----|\n| 1.1 | `sodium_version_string` | any call | [ ] |\n| 1.2 | `sodium_library_version_major` / `sodium_library_version_minor` | any call → `SODIUM_LIBRARY_VERSION_MAJOR == 30`, `MINOR == 0` | [ ] |\n| 1.3 | `sodium_library_minimal` | `SODIUM_LIBRARY_MINIMAL` **undefined** in this build → the `#else` arm → `0` | [ ] |\n| 1.4 | `sodium_init` | very first call in the process (`initialized == 0`) → runs all `_pick_best_implementation` hooks + `randombytes_stir()` + `_sodium_alloc_init()` → `0` | [ ] |\n| 1.5 | `sodium_init` | second and subsequent calls (`initialized != 0`) → early-out → `1` | [ ] |\n| 1.6 | `sodium_init` | called *after* a lazily-initialising randombytes call (e.g. `randombytes_buf` first) — `randombytes_stir()` runs a second time on an already-stirred implementation | [ ] |\n| 1.7 | `sodium_crit_enter` / `sodium_crit_leave` | no-op `#else` implementations: enter-then-leave, leave without enter, nested enter, leave twice — all `0`, no `locked` bookkeeping | [ ] |\n| 1.8 | `sodium_set_misuse_handler` | `handler == NULL` (clears the handler) → a later `sodium_misuse()` goes straight to `abort()` | [ ] |\n| 1.9 | `sodium_set_misuse_handler` | `handler != NULL` → a later `sodium_misuse()` calls the handler first, then `abort()` (handler cannot prevent the abort by returning) | [ ] |\n| 1.10 | `sodium_set_misuse_handler` | called twice — second handler replaces the first | [ ] |\n| 1.11 | `_sodium_runtime_get_cpu_features` | first call vs. repeated calls; `_cpu_features.initialized` set to 1 either way; return value always `-1` | [ ] |\n| 1.12 | `sodium_runtime_has_*` (all 12) | queried before `sodium_init()` (static zero state) vs. after `sodium_init()` (still all zero, since both probes bail out early) — must be identical | [ ] |\n\n### utils.c — memzero / stackzero\n\n| # | entry point(s) | configuration (options set + input shape) | [ ] |\n|---|----------------|--------------------------------------------|-----|\n| 1.13 | `sodium_memzero` | `len == 0` → the volatile `while (i < len)` loop body never executes; `pnt` is never dereferenced (a dangling/NULL `pnt` with `len == 0` is safe) | [ ] |\n| 1.14 | `sodium_memzero` | `len == 1` | [ ] |\n| 1.15 | `sodium_memzero` | `len` not a multiple of the word size (e.g. 7, 17, 31) — the compiled path is a byte-at-a-time volatile loop, so no alignment special-casing | [ ] |\n| 1.16 | `sodium_memzero` | `len` large (e.g. 4096) and/or a sub-slice of a larger buffer — bytes outside `[pnt, pnt+len)` must be untouched | [ ] |\n| 1.17 | `sodium_stackzero` | any `len` including 0 — compiled body is **empty** (no `HAVE_C_VARARRAYS`, no `HAVE_ALLOCA`); observable behaviour is \"does nothing\" | [ ] |\n\n### utils.c — constant-time compare / is_zero\n\n| # | entry point(s) | configuration (options set + input shape) | [ ] |\n|---|----------------|--------------------------------------------|-----|\n| 1.18 | `sodium_memcmp` | `len == 0` → `d` stays 0 → `0` (equal), pointers never dereferenced | [ ] |\n| 1.19 | `sodium_memcmp` | `len == 1`, equal | [ ] |\n| 1.20 | `sodium_memcmp` | `b1_ == b2_` (same pointer), `len > 0` → `0` | [ ] |\n| 1.21 | `sodium_memcmp` | equal buffers at the crypto-relevant sizes 16 / 32 / 64 | [ ] |\n| 1.22 | `sodium_memcmp` | differ only in byte 0 / only in the last byte / in every byte → `-1` in all cases | [ ] |\n| 1.23 | `sodium_memcmp` | `b1` all-`0x00` vs `b2` all-`0xff` → `-1` (exercises the `(d - 1) >> 8` sentinel with `d == 0xff`) | [ ] |\n| 1.24 | `sodium_compare` | `len == 0` → `gt == 0`, `eq == 1` → `0` | [ ] |\n| 1.25 | `sodium_compare` | equal buffers, `len` 1 / 8 / 32 → `0` | [ ] |\n| 1.26 | `sodium_compare` | differ only in the **highest** index (most significant, little-endian) — `b1 < b2` → `-1`; swapped → `1` | [ ] |\n| 1.27 | `sodium_compare` | differ only in index 0 (least significant) — proves little-endian ordering, not `memcmp` ordering | [ ] |\n| 1.28 | `sodium_compare` | `b1` all-`0x00` vs `b2` all-`0xff` → `-1`; and `0xff…` vs `0x00…` → `1` | [ ] |\n| 1.29 | `sodium_compare` | `len` 8 / 12 / 24 / 32 / 64 — the `HAVE_AMD64_ASM` fast paths are **not** compiled, so all lengths take the identical portable loop; verify no length is special | [ ] |\n| 1.30 | `sodium_is_zero` | `nlen == 0` → `1` (vacuously zero) | [ ] |\n| 1.31 | `sodium_is_zero` | all-zero buffer, `nlen` 1 / 16 / 32 → `1` | [ ] |\n| 1.32 | `sodium_is_zero` | single non-zero byte at index 0 / at the last index / `0x01` only → `0` | [ ] |\n| 1.33 | `sodium_is_zero` | all-`0xff` → `0` | [ ] |\n\n### utils.c — increment / add / sub (portable loop only; the `HAVE_AMD64_ASM` 8/12/24/64-byte paths are NOT compiled)\n\n| # | entry point(s) | configuration (options set + input shape) | [ ] |\n|---|----------------|--------------------------------------------|-----|\n| 1.34 | `sodium_increment` | `nlen == 0` → no-op, `n` never dereferenced | [ ] |\n| 1.35 | `sodium_increment` | `nlen == 1`, `n == {0x00}` → `{0x01}` | [ ] |\n| 1.36 | `sodium_increment` | `nlen == 1`, `n == {0xff}` → `{0x00}` (wrap, carry dropped) | [ ] |","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b566403e-4c11-4a9b-ad3a-d43b1f08afd2","uuid":"3de9d510-40f1-464a-968c-52b5e95737fe","timestamp":"2026-08-31T03:47:40.745Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"## Area