{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01QjbHmJFjtmmvCioXetBCSo","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t## Area 8 — crypto_pwhash + crypto_ipcrypt\n2\t\n3\tConfiguration surface of **valid** (non-rejecting) inputs for\n4\t`crypto_pwhash/crypto_pwhash.c`, `crypto_pwhash/argon2/*`,\n5\t`crypto_pwhash/scryptsalsa208sha256/*` (incl. `nosse/`), and\n6\t`crypto_ipcrypt/{crypto_ipcrypt.c, ipcrypt_soft.c}`.\n7\t\n8\tAxes extracted from the source:\n9\t\n10\t* **alg**: `crypto_pwhash_ALG_ARGON2I13` (1) vs `crypto_pwhash_ALG_ARGON2ID13` (2);\n11\t  `crypto_pwhash_ALG_DEFAULT` is an alias of `ARGON2ID13`. Internally `argon2_type` ∈\n12\t  {`Argon2_i`=1, `Argon2_id`=2} (Argon2_d is not compiled in).\n13\t* **entry-point layer**: high-level `crypto_pwhash*` / `crypto_pwhash_argon2i*` /\n14\t  `crypto_pwhash_argon2id*` (which hard-wire `lanes = threads = 1`,\n15\t  `saltlen = 16`, `STR_HASHBYTES = 32`) **and** the low-level `argon2_ctx`, `argon2_hash`,\n16\t  `argon2i_hash_raw`, `argon2id_hash_raw`, `argon2i_hash_encoded`, `argon2id_hash_encoded`,\n17\t  `argon2_verify`, `argon2i_verify`, `argon2id_verify`, `argon2_encode_string`,\n18\t  `argon2_decode_string` (which expose lanes/threads/secret/ad/flags).\n19\t* **lanes / threads**: `lanes ∈ {1, 2, 4, …}`, `threads` independent of `lanes`\n20\t  (`argon2_fill_memory_blocks` is single-threaded regardless — `threads` only affects validation,\n21\t  never the output).\n22\t* **m_cost**: at `8 * lanes` (the effective minimum), just above it, and moderate values;\n23\t  `segment_length = m_cost / (lanes * 4)` and `m_cost` is then re-rounded down to\n24\t  `segment_length * lanes * 4`, so several distinct `m_cost` values collapse to identical work.\n25\t* **t_cost**: 1 (single pass, `fill_block`), 2 and 3 (extra passes take the\n26\t  `fill_block_with_xor` + `pass != 0` branch of `index_alpha`).\n27\t* **outlen**: `ARGON2_MIN_OUTLEN` = 16, typical 24/32, `64` (= `blake2b_BYTES_MAX`, last value on\n28\t  the short `blake2b_long` path), `65`/`128`/`1024` (long path with the 32-byte-per-iteration loop).\n29\t* **pwd / salt / secret / ad**: present vs absent (`NULL` + len 0) and at their minimum lengths\n30\t  (`pwd` min 0, `salt` min 8, `secret` min 0, `ad` min 0).\n31\t* **flags**: `ARGON2_DEFAULT_FLAGS`, `ARGON2_FLAG_CLEAR_PASSWORD`, `ARGON2_FLAG_CLEAR_SECRET`, both.\n32\t* **scrypt**: `N ∈ {2, 16, 512, 1024, 16384}`, `r ∈ {1, 8}`, `p ∈ {1, 2, 512}`; the two branches of\n33\t  `pickparams` (`opslimit < memlimit/32` vs not); the `$7$` setting round trip.\n34\t* **ipcrypt**: deterministic / ND / NDX / PFX, encrypt and decrypt, IPv4-mapped vs pure IPv6\n35\t  16-byte inputs, distinct vs identical key halves.\n36\t\n37\t**Speed note:** every argon2 row below uses `m_cost` ≤ 64 KiB (`memlimit` ≤ 65536) and\n38\t`t_cost` ≤ 3 unless the row explicitly says otherwise, and every scrypt row uses `N ≤ 16384, r ≤ 8,\n39\tp ≤ 2` unless stated, so the whole table runs in well under a second per row. Rows marked\n40\t**(SLOW — optional)** use the documented INTERACTIVE/MODERATE/SENSITIVE presets and should be run at\n41\tmost once each, or skipped in fast CI.\n42\t\n43\t| # | entry point(s) | configuration (options set + input shape) | [ ] |\n44\t|---|----------------|--------------------------------------------|-----|\n45\t| 8.1 | `crypto_pwhash_alg_argon2i13`, `crypto_pwhash_alg_argon2id13`, `crypto_pwhash_alg_default` | no input; must return 1, 2, 2 respectively (`ALG_DEFAULT == ALG_ARGON2ID13`) | [ ] |\n46\t| 8.2 | `crypto_pwhash_bytes_min`/`_max`, `_passwd_min`/`_max`, `_saltbytes`, `_strbytes`, `_strprefix`, `_primitive` | no input; 16 / 4294967295 / 0 / 4294967295 / 16 / 128 / `\"$argon2id$\"` / `\"argon2id,argon2i\"` | [ ] |\n47\t| 8.3 | `crypto_pwhash_opslimit_min`/`_max`/`_interactive`/`_moderate`/`_sensitive`, `crypto_pwhash_memlimit_min`/`_max`/`_interactive`/`_moderate`/`_sensitive` | no input; 1 / 4294967295 / 2 / 3 / 4 and 8192 / 4398046510080 / 67108864 / 268435456 / 1073741824 (all alias the argon2id values) | [ ] |\n48\t| 8.4 | `crypto_pwhash_argon2i_*` constant getters (alg, bytes_min/max, passwd_min/max, saltbytes, strbytes, strprefix, opslimit_min/max/interactive/moderate/sensitive, memlimit_min/max/interactive/moderate/sensitive) | no input; 1 / 16 / 4294967295 / 0 / 4294967295 / 16 / 128 / `\"$argon2i$\"` / 3,4294967295,4,6,8 / 8192,4398046510080,33554432,134217728,536870912 | [ ] |\n49\t| 8.5 | `crypto_pwhash_argon2id_*` constant getters (same list) | no input; 2 / 16 / 4294967295 / 0 / 4294967295 / 16 / 128 / `\"$argon2id$\"` / 1,4294967295,2,3,4 / 8192,4398046510080,67108864,268435456,1073741824 | [ ] |\n50\t| 8.6 | `crypto_pwhash` | `alg = ALG_ARGON2I13`, `opslimit = 3` (`argon2i_OPSLIMIT_MIN`), `memlimit = 8192` (`MEMLIMIT_MIN` → `m_cost = 8`), `outlen = 16` (`BYTES_MIN`), `passwd = \"test\"` (len 4), 16-byte salt; fast | [ ] |\n51\t| 8.7 | `crypto_pwhash` | `alg = ALG_ARGON2I13`, `opslimit = 3`, `memlimit = 8192`, `outlen = 32` | [ ] |\n52\t| 8.8 | `crypto_pwhash` | `alg = ALG_ARGON2I13`, `opslimit = 4`, `memlimit = 16384` (`m_cost = 16`), `outlen = 64` (last short `blake2b_long` size) | [ ] |\n53\t| 8.9 | `crypto_pwhash` | `alg = ALG_ARGON2I13`, `opslimit = 3`, `memlimit = 65536` (`m_cost = 64`), `outlen = 65` (first long `blake2b_long` size) | [ ] |\n54\t| 8.10 | `crypto_pwhash` | `alg = ALG_ARGON2ID13`, `opslimit = 1` (`argon2id_OPSLIMIT_MIN`), `memlimit = 8192`, `outlen = 16` | [ ] |\n55\t| 8.11 | `crypto_pwhash` | `alg = ALG_ARGON2ID13`, `opslimit = 2`, `memlimit = 8192`, `outlen = 32` (two passes: pass 1 is fully data-dependent) | [ ] |\n56\t| 8.12 | `crypto_pwhash` | `alg = ALG_ARGON2ID13`, `opslimit = 3`, `memlimit = 32768` (`m_cost = 32`), `outlen = 32` | [ ] |\n57\t| 8.13 | `crypto_pwhash` | `alg = ALG_DEFAULT`, `opslimit = 1`, `memlimit = 8192`, `outlen = 16`; output must be byte-identical to row 8.10 (`ALG_DEFAULT == ARGON2ID13`) | [ ] |\n58\t| 8.14 | `crypto_pwhash` | `alg = ALG_ARGON2ID13`, `outlen = 128` and `outlen = 1024` (multi-iteration long `blake2b_long` path), `opslimit = 1`, `memlimit = 8192` | [ ] |\n59\t| 8.15 | `crypto_pwhash` | `passwdlen = 0` with a non-NULL `passwd` pointer (`PASSWD_MIN` is 0), `alg = ALG_ARGON2ID13`, `opslimit = 1`, `memlimit = 8192`, `outlen = 16` | [ ] |\n60\t| 8.16 | `crypto_pwhash` | `passwdlen = 1`; then a long password (e.g. 256 bytes, and one > 128 bytes containing NUL and 0xFF bytes — password is binary, not a C string) | [ ] |\n61\t| 8.17 | `crypto_pwhash` | `memlimit` not a multiple of 1024: `memlimit = 8192 + 512` and `9215` both truncate to `m_cost = 8` → output identical to row 8.10 | [ ] |\n62\t| 8.18 | `crypto_pwhash` | salt values: all-zero 16 bytes, all-0xFF 16 bytes, random; salt length is fixed at `crypto_pwhash_SALTBYTES` = 16 by the wrapper | [ ] |\n63\t| 8.19 | `crypto_pwhash` **(SLOW — optional)** | `alg = ALG_ARGON2ID13`, `opslimit = crypto_pwhash_OPSLIMIT_INTERACTIVE` (2), `memlimit = crypto_pwhash_MEMLIMIT_INTERACTIVE` (67108864 → `m_cost = 65536`), `outlen = 32` — the documented interactive preset; ~64 MiB allocation | [ ] |\n64\t| 8.20 | `crypto_pwhash` **(SLOW — optional)** | `alg = ALG_ARGON2I13`, `opslimit = crypto_pwhash_argon2i_OPSLIMIT_INTERACTIVE` (4), `memlimit = 33554432` (`m_cost = 32768`), `outlen = 32` | [ ] |\n65\t| 8.21 | `crypto_pwhash_argon2i` (direct) | `alg = crypto_pwhash_argon2i_ALG_ARGON2I13`, `opslimit = 3`, `memlimit = 8192`, `outlen = 16`; must equal `crypto_pwhash` with `ALG_ARGON2I13` (row 8.6 shape) | [ ] |\n66\t| 8.22 | `crypto_pwhash_argon2id` (direct) | `alg = crypto_pwhash_argon2id_ALG_ARGON2ID13`, `opslimit = 1`, `memlimit = 8192`, `outlen = 16`; must equal row 8.10 | [ ] |\n67\t| 8.23 | `crypto_pwhash_str` | `passwd = \"password\"`, `opslimit = crypto_pwhash_OPSLIMIT_MIN` (1), `memlimit = crypto_pwhash_MEMLIMIT_MIN` (8192) — deliberately minimal so the test is fast. Output: 128-byte buffer, `\"$argon2id$v=19$m=8,t=1,p=1$\"` + 22 base64 chars + `\"$\"` + 43 base64 c