e whole state, so double-`final` and update-after-`final` silently hash from a\n  zeroed state and still return 0 — assert C and Rust agree on that exact behaviour\n- accessors `crypto_hash_bytes`, `crypto_hash_primitive`, `crypto_hash_sha256_bytes`,\n  `crypto_hash_sha512_bytes`, `crypto_hash_statebytes`\n- out-of-bounds-write detection with `padded(len)` / `check_pad(...)` on every output buffer\n\nRULES (absolute):\n- `$ROOT/c_src/` is READ-ONLY ground truth. NEVER modify it. The C is ALWAYS correct.\n- Run cargo from `$ROOT/translation` and ALWAYS pass `--offline` (no network). Use\n  `timeout 600 cargo ...`.\n- All calls go through `libloading` + `dlsym` on BOTH .so files — never call Rust directly.\n- Harness `$ROOT/translation/tests/common/mod.rs` provides `both::<FnType>(\"sym\")`,\n  `has(\"sym\")`, `eqb`, `eqi`, `hex`, `Rng::new(seed)`, `padded`/`check_pad`, `rng_reset`,\n  `errno`/`set_errno`, `eq_abort`. Read `$ROOT/translation/tests/a1_utils.rs` for style.\n- On divergence the C is right: fix `$ROOT/translation/src/*.rs` surgically (other agents are\n  editing other modules concurrently — touch only what you must, never reformat).\n\nFinish with `timeout 600 cargo test --offline --test a3_sha2` at 0 failures. Then tick the\nSHA-2 rows of `configs_3.md` `[ ]` → `[x]` and append a status value (`verified` /\n`unreachable-from-public-API`) to the SHA-2 rows of `errors_3.md` ONLY.\nReport: test count, rows checked off, divergences found+fixed, gaps+reasons."}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":838,"cache_read_input_tokens":266979,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":838,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":17,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b566403e-4c11-4a9b-ad3a-d43b1f08afd2","uuid":"aea7e532-03b8-436e-b21b-e21430dcfedc","timestamp":"2026-08-31T03:55:46.721Z"}
