{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01AeQZWyp3ofqan15QWSpJGw","type":"tool_result","content":"configs_1.md\nconfigs_2.md\nconfigs_3.md\nconfigs_4.md\nconfigs_5.md\nconfigs_6.md\nconfigs_7.md\nconfigs_8.md\nerrors_1.md\nerrors_2.md\nerrors_3.md\nerrors_4.md\nerrors_5.md\nerrors_6.md\nerrors_7.md\nerrors_8.md\n=== configs_3 ===\n## Area 3 — hashes / xof / generichash / shorthash\n\nScope: `crypto_hash/{crypto_hash.c, sha256/**, sha512/**, sha3/hash_sha3.c}`, `crypto_xof/**`,\n`crypto_generichash/{crypto_generichash.c, blake2b/generichash_blake2.c, blake2b/ref/**}`,\n`crypto_shorthash/**` + public headers.\n\nBuild assumption: no `HAVE_*` macros are defined, so every `#ifdef HAVE_*` takes the portable fallback\n(`SHA256_Transform` scalar path, `blake2b_compress_ref`, non-`HAVE_TI_MODE` counter increment).\n\nBlock / rate sizes that drive the boundary axes:\n\n| primitive | block or rate | source |\n|---|---|---|\n| SHA-256 | 64 B block | `hash_sha256_cp.c` (`& 0x3f`, pad threshold 56) |\n| SHA-512 | 128 B block | `hash_sha512_cp.c` (`& 0x7f`, pad threshold 112) |\n| SHA3-256 | 136 B rate | `SHA3_256_RATE` |\n| SHA3-512 | 72 B rate | `SHA3_512_RATE` |\n| SHAKE128 / TurboSHAKE128 | 168 B rate | `SHAKE128_RATE` / `TURBOSHAKE128_RATE` |\n| SHAKE256 / TurboSHAKE256 | 136 B rate | `SHAKE256_RATE` / `TURBOSHAKE256_RATE` |\n| BLAKE2b | 128 B block, 256 B lazy buffer (`buf[2*128]`) | `blake2.h` / `blake2b_update` |\n\n**Length set L** (used by many rows below) = `{0, 1, 63, 64, 65, 127, 128, 129, 135, 136, 137, 143, 144, 255, 256}`.\nIt straddles every block/rate boundary in the area: 63/64/65 (SHA-256), 71/72/73 → covered by 143/144 mod 72,\n127/128/129 (SHA-512, BLAKE2b), 135/136/137 (SHA3-256, SHAKE256, TurboSHAKE256), 143/144 (2×72 for SHA3-512),\n255/256 (2× SHA-512 block, BLAKE2b full buffer).\n\n| # | entry point(s) | configuration (options set + input shape) | [ ] |\n|---|----------------|--------------------------------------------|-----|\n| 3.1 | `crypto_hash` | one-shot, `inlen` over all of L; must equal `crypto_hash_sha512` byte-for-byte (32→64 B out is 64) | [ ] |\n| 3.2 | `crypto_hash_bytes`, `crypto_hash_primitive` | no input; expect `64`, `\"sha512\"` | [ ] |\n| 3.3 | `crypto_hash_sha256` | one-shot, `inlen` over all of L | [ ] |\n| 3.4 | `crypto_hash_sha256_{init,update,final}` | streaming, single `update` of each `inlen` in L | [ ] |\n| 3.5 | `crypto_hash_sha256_*` | streaming, `inlen = 256` fed as 256 separate 1-byte `update` calls (exercises `r` walking 0..63 and the `inlen < 64 - r` lazy branch on every offset) | [ ] |\n| 3.6 | `crypto_hash_sha256_*` | streaming, two updates `(a, b)` for every pair with `a + b` ∈ L and `a` ∈ {0,1,31,32,33,63,64,65}: covers `r != 0` entry, the `for (i = 0; i < 64 - r; i++)` fill-and-transform, and the `inlen &= 63` tail | [ ] |\n| 3.7 | `crypto_hash_sha256_*` | streaming, `update` with `inlen == 0` interleaved between non-empty updates (must be a no-op: `count` unchanged) | [ ] |\n| 3.8 | `crypto_hash_sha256_*` | streaming with `inlen == 64 - r` exactly (update ends exactly on a block boundary → `inlen &= 63` yields 0, `buf` left untouched) | [ ] |\n| 3.9 | `crypto_hash_sha256_*` | `SHA256_Pad` short branch: total length ≡ `r < 56` (mod 64), e.g. 0, 1, 55 | [ ] |\n| 3.10 | `crypto_hash_sha256_*` | `SHA256_Pad` long branch: total length ≡ `r >= 56` (mod 64), e.g. 56, 57, 63, 120, 127 (two-block padding) | [ ] |\n| 3.11 | `crypto_hash_sha256_statebytes` | no input; equals `sizeof(crypto_hash_sha256_state)` | [ ] |\n| 3.12 | `crypto_hash_sha256` vs streaming | equivalence: one-shot == init/update×n/final for every split in 3.6 | [ ] |\n| 3.13 | `crypto_hash_sha512` | one-shot, `inlen` over all of L | [ ] |\n| 3.14 | `crypto_hash_sha512_{init,update,final}` | streaming, single `update` of each `inlen` in L | [ ] |\n| 3.15 | `crypto_hash_sha512_*` | streaming, `inlen = 256` fed as 256 separate 1-byte `update` calls (`r` walks 0..127) | [ ] |\n| 3.16 | `crypto_hash_sha512_*` | streaming, two updates `(a, b)` with `a + b` ∈ L and `a` ∈ {0,1,63,64,65,127,128,129}: covers `r != 0`, the `128 - r` fill, the `while (inlen >= 128)` bulk loop, and `inlen &= 127` | [ ] |\n| 3.17 | `crypto_hash_sha512_*` | `update` with `inlen == 0` interleaved (must not advance `count[0]`/`count[1]`) | [ ] |\n| 3.18 | `crypto_hash_sha512_*` | `SHA512_Pad` short branch: total ≡ `r < 112` (mod 128), e.g. 0, 1, 111 | [ ] |\n| 3.19 | `crypto_hash_sha512_*` | `SHA512_Pad` long branch: total ≡ `r >= 112` (mod 128), e.g. 112, 113, 127, 240, 255 | [ ] |\n| 3.20 | `crypto_hash_sha512_*` | length whose bit count exercises `bitlen[0] = inlen >> 61` ≠ 0 and the `count[1]` carry (conceptual / streaming-accumulated) | [ ] |\n| 3.21 | `crypto_hash_sha512_statebytes` | no input | [ ] |\n| 3.22 | `crypto_hash_sha512` vs streaming | equivalence across every split in 3.16 | [ ] |\n| 3.23 | `crypto_hash_sha3256` | one-shot, `inlen` over all of L plus `{71, 72, 73, 167, 168, 271, 272, 273}` (rate 136 and 2×136) | [ ] |\n| 3.24 | `crypto_hash_sha3256_{init,update,final}` | streaming, single `update` of each `inlen` above | [ ] |\n| 3.25 | `crypto_hash_sha3256_*` | streaming, 1-byte updates ×272 (drives `state->offset` 0..136 twice, incl. `offset == rate` re-permute at the head of `sha3_update`) | [ ] |\n| 3.26 | `crypto_hash_sha3256_*` | streaming, two updates `(a, b)` with `a` ∈ {1, 135, 136, 137} and `a + b` ∈ {136, 137, 272, 273}: hits the `offset != 0 && inlen > 0` partial-chunk arm, the `offset == rate && consumed < inlen` mid-permute, the `while (inlen - consumed >= rate)` bulk arm, and the trailing `consumed < inlen` arm | [ ] |\n| 3.27 | `crypto_hash_sha3256_*` | streaming, `update(inlen = 0)` first and between updates (must not permute; `offset` unchanged) | [ ] |\n| 3.28 | `crypto_hash_sha3256_*` | total input ≡ `rate - 1` (135) mod 136 → `sha3_final` fused pad byte `0x06 ^ 0x80 == 0x86` | [ ] |\n| 3.29 | `crypto_hash_sha3256_*` | total input ≡ 0 m