{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_pvoylf5wtkq77pk4fdv3mitjl7ih6yrzjkjvdcygranpxbx6qz5q","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Area 4 is complete and green.\n\n## Files\n\n**Created** `$ROOT/translation/tests/a4_onetimeauth.rs` — 20 tests, all passing (`crypto_onetimeauth*` + `crypto_onetimeauth_poly1305*`, donna32 backend).\n\n**Edited (surgical)**\n- `$ROOT/translation/tests/a4_hmac.rs` — added a file-local `RNG_LOCK` mutex taken by the 4 `*_keygen` tests (see \"flaky test fixed\" below). No other change.\n- `$ROOT/translation/phaseA/configs_4.md` — all 182 rows `[ ]` → `[x]`.\n- `$ROOT/translation/phaseA/errors_4.md` — new trailing `status` column on all 24 rows.\n- Regenerated `CONFIGS.md` / `ERRORS.md` via `build-phaseA.sh` (area 4 now reads **182 rows / 182 checked**).\n\n`$ROOT/c_src/` untouched. `$ROOT/translation/src/poly1305.rs` is byte-identical to how I found it (only temporarily mutated for a negative control, then restored and verified).\n\n## Test coverage (a4_onetimeauth.rs)\n\n`accessors`, `donna32_state_layout_after_init`, `donna32_leftover_field_tracking`, `oneshot_named_lengths`, `oneshot_all_lengths_0_to_300`, `streaming_single_update_named_lengths`, `streaming_single_update_0_to_300`, `leftover_branch_fixed_splits`, `many_one_byte_updates`, `zero_length_updates`, `randomized_splits_0_to_300`, `long_messages`, `key_shapes`, `verify_good_and_every_corruption`, `verify_streaming_tags_sweep`, `keygen`, `generic_oneshot_and_verify`, `generic_streaming_and_crossmixing`, `pick_best_implementation_is_a_no_op`, `poly1305_randomized_fuzz`.\n\nNotable strength beyond the brief:\n- The **full 256-byte opaque state** is compared after `init` and after *every* `update` (and after `final`, where `sodium_memzero` must have wiped the 144-byte internal struct).\n- Two tests decode the raw state as the donna32 struct and assert the actual field values: the five clamped 26-bit `r` limbs, `h==0`, `pad[4]`, `leftover`, the live prefix of `buffer[16]`, `final`, and that bytes 144..256 are never touched. This would fail if the port had used the donna64 (3-limb) layout.\n- `leftover` is asserted against an explicit expected value after each chunk for all named branch shapes: `(1,15) (15,1) (8,8) (15,2) (16,1) (17,16) (5,11) (5,40) (5,27)`, 17×1-byte, and zero-length updates at every leftover value 1..15.\n- RFC 8439 §2.5.2 known-answer test (absolute, not just C==Rust), one-shot and streaming.\n- All 8 generic/primitive `init`/`update`/`final` cross-mix combinations, plus alternating generic and primitive `update` calls on one live state, with intermediate states compared against the pure poly1305 run.\n- `verify` corruption: every one of the 16 bytes × 8 bits, plus 4 whole-byte deltas per byte, per length.\n\n## Divergences\n\n**None in the Rust translation.** `src/poly1305.rs` matched C byte-for-byte on every configuration, including full-state equality.\n\nTwo test-side issues found and fixed:\n\n1. **My own bad assumption** (initial failure): I asserted that flipping bit 7 of key byte 15 must make `verify` reject. Both C *and* Rust returned `0` — correct, because Poly1305's `r` clamp (`0x0ffffffc0ffffffc0ffffffc0fffffff`) discards the high 4 bits of key bytes 3/7/11/15 and the low 2 bits of bytes 4/8/12, and for an empty message no bit of `key[0..16]` affects the tag at all. Rewritten as a **clamp-aware** sweep over all 32 key bytes × 8 bits asserting `0` exactly for the discarded bits and `-1` otherwise — a much stronger check that now pins the exact clamp mask in both libraries.\n\n2. **Pre-existing flaky test in `a4_hmac.rs`** (not a regression — reproduced ~1 in 3 runs before I touched anything): the four `*_keygen` tests call `rng_reseed()` then interleave C/Rust `randombytes_buf` calls, but `common::RNG_STATE` is process-global and `cargo test` runs them on separate threads, so one test's reseed lands between another's C and Rust call. Fixed with a file-local mutex. 6 consecutive runs now pass (was 4/6).\n\n## Negative control\n\nTo prove the suite really bites, I temporarily changed one bit of one mask in `src/poly1305.rs` (`0x3ffff03` → `0x3ffff02`) and rebuilt: **14 of 20 tests failed**, including the state-layout test. Reverted and re-verified.\n\n## Gaps and reasons\n\n- `errors_4` **4.3 / 4.6 / 4.9** — `unreachable-from-public-API`: the `-(h == correct)` aliasing term compares the caller's pointer to a fresh stack local, so it is always 0. Not synthesizable through `dlsym`.\n- `errors_4` **4.16 / 4.17** — `undefined-behaviour-not-tested`: `key == NULL` with `keylen > BLOCKBYTES` skips `sodium_misuse()` and NULL-derefs inside `crypto_hash_sha*_update`. Deliberately not exercised.\n- All other 19 error rows and all 182 config rows are `verified`.\n\n## Note for whoever runs the suite next\n\n`cargo test --offline --test <name>` does **not** rebuild the `cdylib` (the test target has no Rust-level dependency on it — everything goes through `dlsym`). You must run `cargo build --offline` first, or you are testing a stale `target/debug/liblibsodium.so`. This silently masked my first negative-control attempt."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":601,"cache_read_input_tokens":153399,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":601,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01A8Z33Vq9d29RKVTuGuAUQG","session_id":"b566403e-4c11-4a9b-ad3a-d43b1f08afd2","uuid":"99d4c452-0645-471b-8a7f-af22899965e3","timestamp":"2026-08-31T04:07:01.713Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Resume area 4: onetimeauth"}
