{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_62guhd5mzxdlrmwg44py7bofok3iuonzivdxf3kkvkxa3dsdt7xa","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Area 6 Phase B + C complete — all green, zero divergences found.\n\n## Files created\n- `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-RqaJY6/translation/tests/a6_aead.rs` — 21 tests (aegis128l, aegis256, chacha20poly1305, chacha20poly1305_ietf, xchacha20poly1305_ietf)\n- `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-RqaJY6/translation/tests/a6_aes256gcm.rs` — 10 tests (the ENOSYS stub family)\n- `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-RqaJY6/translation/tests/a6_secretbox.rs` — 17 tests\n- `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-RqaJY6/translation/tests/a6_secretstream.rs` — 21 tests\n\n**69 test functions, 0 failures**, stable across repeated runs.\n\n## Rows checked off\n- `phaseA/configs_6.md`: all **129** rows `[ ]` → `[x]`, plus an appended \"Coverage notes\" section.\n- `phaseA/errors_6.md`: all **84** rows annotated with a new `status` column — 81 `verified`, 2 `unreachable-from-public-API` (6.10 / 6.20, the internal `aegis*_mac` `maclen ∉ {16,32}` branch), 1 `undefined-behaviour-not-tested` (6.79, `_pull` with `m == NULL && mlen > 0` is a NULL deref in C).\n\n## Divergences found and fixed\n**None.** The area-6 Rust modules (`aead_aegis128l.rs`, `aead_aegis256.rs`, `aead_aes256gcm.rs`, `aead_chacha20poly1305.rs`, `aead_xchacha20poly1305.rs`, `secretbox.rs`, `secretstream.rs`) match the C bit-for-bit on everything tested, including the quirky secretstream Poly1305 padding `(0x10 - sizeof block + mlen) & 0xf`, the `slen = 64 + mlen` length field, the aes256gcm \"`*clen_p`/`*mlen_p`/`*maclen_p` left UNWRITTEN\" behaviour (distinct from every other AEAD, which stores 0), and the zero-on-failure asymmetry (AEAD `_decrypt_detached` memsets `m`; secretbox `_open_detached` and secretstream `_pull` do not). No `src/` file was modified.\n\nI ran three **negative controls** (mutating the secretstream padding expression, the aegis128l failure memset, and the secretbox `mlen0` clamp) to prove the suites are sensitive — each mutation was caught, and all sources were restored byte-identically afterwards.\n\n## Notable coverage details\n- Every AEAD: combined + detached, `ad` NULL / non-NULL-empty / 1..33, `mlen` sweep 0..=300 plus family-specific big sets (up to 262145 crossing the `STREAM_POLY1305_CHUNK == 131072` restart), NULL and non-NULL out-length pointers, in-place aliasing, all-zero/all-0xff keys and nonces, tag corrupted in **every** byte position, `clen ∈ {ABYTES-1, ABYTES, ABYTES+1}`, `nsec` non-NULL/poisoned, and C↔Rust ciphertext interop both directions. Guard bytes past every output buffer.\n- Real absolute KAT: RFC 8439 §2.8.2 tag for `chacha20poly1305_ietf`. Structural pins: `xchacha20poly1305_ietf == chacha20poly1305_ietf` under `hchacha20`, and both secretbox families re-derived from `hsalsa20`/`hchacha20` + stream + Poly1305 primitives.\n- secretstream: the **full 52-byte opaque state** is compared between C and Rust after *every* `init_push`/`init_pull`/`push`/`pull`/`rekey`; all 256 tag byte values driven through `_push`; white-box 32-bit counter wrap; exact-`statebytes()` allocation at 4 offsets with under/over-write guards; `sodium_misuse()` aborts via `eq_abort`.\n\n## Could not cover\n1. **`crypto_aead_xchacha20poly1305_IETF_*` uppercase aliases** (row 6.65) — preprocessor macros in the header, not exported symbols, so unreachable via `dlsym`.\n2. **`m == NULL` with `mlen > 0` in `_pull`** (errors 6.79) — genuine NULL deref in C; only the safe `mlen == 0` case is exercised.\n3. **`mlen > MESSAGEBYTES_MAX` on the three chacha `_encrypt_detached`** (errors 6.45) — those have no guard, so the trigger would be an out-of-bounds read. Verified instead as *absence of any rejection* across the whole valid sweep.\n4. **Internal `aegis*_mac` with `maclen ∉ {16,32}`** (errors 6.10/6.20) — `maclen` is hard-wired to 32 at every call site.\n\nOne harness note for other agents: `common::rng_reseed`/`rng_reset` manipulate a **process-global** RNG state, so tests in the same binary that both consume library randomness race under cargo's default parallelism. I serialize those sections with a file-local `Mutex` in `a6_secretstream.rs`; `tests/a1_randombytes.rs` calls `rng_reset()` from four separate `#[test]` functions without any such guard and looks latently flaky."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":564,"cache_read_input_tokens":223579,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":564,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01G8XLQhMZMM1EHkKTrfCEmQ","session_id":"b566403e-4c11-4a9b-ad3a-d43b1f08afd2","uuid":"1a641144-708a-419e-970c-10ea4cc567ac","timestamp":"2026-08-31T04:08:13.186Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Phase B/C tests area 6"}
