{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01PLixuVAqhYNfWJ2zncoRyp","type":"tool_result","content":"## Area 1 — sodium core + randombytes\n\nBuild assumed: x86-64 Linux, CMake defines **no** `HAVE_*` macros, `-std=c99`, **no `-DNDEBUG`** (so `assert()` is live).\nDerived macros that *are* active: `__linux__`, `__x86_64__`, `HAVE_LINUX_COMPATIBLE_GETRANDOM` (derived from `__linux__` + `SYS_getrandom`/`__NR_getrandom` via `syscall()`), `BLOCK_ON_DEV_RANDOM`, `DEFAULT_PAGE_SIZE 0x10000`, `ENOSYS`.\nDerived macros that are **NOT** active: `HAVE_ALIGNED_MALLOC`, `HAVE_PAGE_PROTECTION`, `HAVE_MPROTECT`, `HAVE_MLOCK`, `HAVE_MMAP`/`MAP_ANON`, `HAVE_POSIX_MEMALIGN`, `HAVE_WEAK_SYMBOLS`, `HAVE_AMD64_ASM`, `HAVE_CPUID`, `HAVE_RDRAND`, `HAVE_GETPID`, `HAVE_GETENTROPY`, `HAVE_PTHREAD`, `HAVE_ATOMIC_OPS`, `HAVE_C_VARARRAYS`/`HAVE_ALLOCA`, `WINAPI_DESKTOP`, `NONEXISTENT_DEV_RANDOM`, `HAVE_SAFE_ARC4RANDOM`, `TLS` (empty → `stream` in randombytes_internal_random.c is a plain global, **not** thread-local).\n\n| # | function | trigger (exact invalid input/condition) | expected C result | status |\n|---|----------|------------------------------------------|-------------------|-------|\n| 1.1 | `sodium_crit_enter` | any call — `#else` no-op branch is compiled (no `_WIN32`, no `HAVE_PTHREAD`, no `HAVE_ATOMIC_OPS`) | never fails: always `0`; the `assert(locked == 0)` and `errno=EPERM` paths are **not compiled** | verified |\n| 1.2 | `sodium_crit_leave` | any call, including leave-without-enter | never fails: always `0` (the `locked == 0` → `-1`/`EPERM` branch is not compiled) | verified |\n| 1.3 | `sodium_init` | `sodium_crit_enter() != 0` (entry lock failure) | `-1`; **unreachable** in this build (1.1) | not-compiled-in-this-build |\n| 1.4 | `sodium_init` | called a 2nd or later time (`initialized != 0`) | `1` (distinct non-error sentinel, not `0`) | verified |\n| 1.5 | `sodium_init` | `sodium_crit_leave() != 0` on the already-initialized path | `-1`; **unreachable** (1.2) | not-compiled-in-this-build |\n| 1.6 | `sodium_init` | `sodium_crit_leave() != 0` after first-time init | `-1`; **unreachable** (1.2) | not-compiled-in-this-build |\n| 1.7 | `sodium_misuse` | reached from any misuse site | aborts (sodium_misuse) — calls the installed `_misuse_handler` first (if non-NULL), then unconditional `abort()`; `noreturn` | verified |\n| 1.8 | `sodium_set_misuse_handler` | `sodium_crit_enter() != 0` | `-1`; **unreachable** (1.1) | not-compiled-in-this-build |\n| 1.9 | `sodium_set_misuse_handler` | `sodium_crit_leave() != 0` after storing the handler | `-1`; **unreachable** (1.2) | not-compiled-in-this-build |\n| 1.10 | `_sodium_runtime_arm_cpu_features` | `__ARM_ARCH` undefined (x86-64) → unconditional `#ifndef __ARM_ARCH return -1` | always `-1`, after setting `has_neon = has_armcrypto = 0` | verified-indirectly (static fn; observed through its public callers) |\n| 1.11 | `_sodium_runtime_intel_cpu_features` | `HAVE_CPUID` undefined → `_cpuid()` zero-fills `cpu_info`, so `cpu_info[0] == 0U` | always `-1`, taken **before** any `has_*` field is assigned (all stay statically zero) | verified-indirectly (static fn; observed through its public callers) |\n| 1.12 | `_sodium_runtime_get_cpu_features` | both sub-probes return `-1`; `ret = -1 & -1 & -1` | always `-1` (return value is ignored by `sodium_init`); `_cpu_features.initialized = 1` is still set | verified |\n----\nconfigs_1.md\nconfigs_2.md\nconfigs_3.md\nconfigs_4.md\nconfigs_5.md\nconfigs_6.md\nconfigs_7.md\nconfigs_8.md\nerrors_1.md\nerrors_2.md\nerrors_3.md\nerrors_4.md\nerrors_5.md\nerrors_6.md\nerrors_7.md\nerrors_8.md","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01Y8KmEUWZuyfELGp9tb2pNF","session_id":"b566403e-4c11-4a9b-ad3a-d43b1f08afd2","uuid":"4617adbb-eac9-43d7-b19e-409e24104e61","timestamp":"2026-08-31T04:08:35.614Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Finish area 2 bookkeeping+gaps"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_o4sfp2rm4cil2lncop7mddnvgdj6yym3t3zukxns6ohlbadcgtea","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Done: `timeout 600 cargo test --offline --test a3_sha3_xof` → 35 tests, 0 failures (~2s).**\n\n## What was written\n\nOne file: `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-RqaJY6/translation/tests/a3_sha3_xof.rs` (35 `#[test]` fns). Nothing under `c_src/` or `src/` was touched.\n\nExact exported symbol families confirmed with `nm -D` on both `.so`s (note the names have **no** underscore before the digits — `crypto_hash_sha3256`, not `crypto_hash_sha3_256`): `crypto_hash_sha3{256,512}{,_init,_update,_final,_bytes,_statebytes}`, `crypto_xof_{shake128,shake256,turboshake128,turboshake256}{,_init,_init_with_domain,_update,_squeeze,_blockbytes,_statebytes,_domain_standard}`, plus the internal `_sodium_{shake,turboshake}{128,256}_ref{,_init,_init_with_domain,_update,_squeeze}` — all exported by **both** libraries, all covered. Everything is gated behind `has()`.\n\n## Coverage highlights\n- One-shot + streaming over inlen `0..=300` (straddles 72/104/136/144/168 ±1) plus 2×/3×/4× rate multiples and multi-KiB up to 8192; four content patterns.\n- **Full 256-byte state comparison** after `init` and after *every* `update`/`final`/`squeeze`, using a `#[repr(C, align(16))]` buffer with `PAD` guard bytes so an over-long write into the state is caught too. Two dedicated tests decode and pin the internal layout (`offset`@224, `rate`@232, `outlen`@240, `phase`@248 for SHA-3; `offset`@224, `phase`@232, `domain`@233 for the XOFs) on both sides, so the state compare is provably load-bearing rather than comparing mostly-zero buffers.\n- Randomized multi-chunk absorb and squeeze splits (fixed seeds), including long runs of 1-byte calls and interleaved zero-length calls; `squeeze(4096)` one-call vs ~9 chunkings.\n- **All 256 domain bytes** through `_init_with_domain` at six absorb offsets (0, mid, `RATE-1` fused pad, `RATE` extra-permute, and the same in the 2nd block); asserts `0` return for every value and 256 pairwise-distinct streams — `0x00` and `0x80` are accepted exactly like any other byte, and the byte is stored verbatim in the state.\n- Error sentinels asserted exactly: `update` after `final`/`squeeze` returns **`-1`** yet still permutes *and* absorbs (proved by diffing against an empty-update reference run); a 2nd/3rd `final` returns **`-1`** but still writes all `outlen` bytes (proved with three different pre-fill patterns giving identical output); `squeeze`-after-`squeeze` is `0` with 40 chained squeezes equalling one long squeeze.\n- `padded()`/`check_pad()` on every output buffer and every state buffer; aliased `out`/`in` one-shots; state re-use after `final`/`squeeze`.\n\n## Divergences found and fixed\n**None.** The Rust port is byte-exact against the C, including the full internal state layout and every `-1` sentinel. No `src/*.rs` edits were needed. (Two initial red tests were my own test-logic bugs: a squeeze-chunk set that didn't total 512, and a wrong inequality assertion — see below.)\n\n## Notable finding\n`crypto_xof_shake256_init_with_domain(state, 0x06)` is **exactly** `crypto_hash_sha3256` (same rate 136, same domain byte, same 24-round permute) — the first 32 squeezed bytes equal the SHA3-256 digest bit for bit. This is now pinned as an equality in `xof_sha3_domain_byte_is_reachable`, together with the inequalities for TurboSHAKE256 (12 rounds, same rate) and SHAKE128 (rate 168). SHA3-512's rate 72 is unreachable from any XOF.\n\n## Rows checked off\n- `phaseA/configs_3.md`: **61 rows** ticked `[ ]` → `[x]` (3.23 – 3.83, the whole sha3 + xof block). The sha2/blake2b/shorthash rows were left alone; rows 3.1–3.22 were already ticked by another agent and are preserved.\n- `phaseA/errors_3.md`: **17 rows** annotated (3.17 – 3.33), all `**status: verified**`. Three carry a qualifier: 3.17 and 3.26 note that the `COMPILER_ASSERT` itself is compile-time (`unreachable-from-public-API`) while the runtime `0` and the 256-byte state size are pinned; 3.25 notes it was verified at both the `_sodium_*_ref_init_with_domain` entry point and the public wrapper.\n\n## Gaps\n- The `COMPILER_ASSERT(sizeof(public_state) >= sizeof(internal_state))` in every `init`/one-shot is compile-time only, so it is unreachable at runtime; the observable consequence (`statebytes() == 256`) is asserted instead.\n- errors_3 row 3.31's note that the `*_ref` one-shot does **not** zero its stack-local state is not externally observable; I confirmed by inspection that `translation/src/xof.rs` matches the C (no `sodium_memzero` there, unlike the SHA-3 one-shot, which does zero and which is exercised).\n- `in == NULL` / `out == NULL` with non-zero length is UB in C for these families (no runtime check, only `__attribute__((nonnull))`), so only the defined `in == NULL, inlen == 0` case is tested.\n- 32-bit `size_t` truncation of the `unsigned long long inlen` (errors_3 rows 3.109/3.28/3.32) is unreachable on this x86-64 target.\n- `crypto_core_keccak1600_*` itself is Area 2's scope and is already covered by `tests/a2_salsa_keccak.rs`; I did not duplicate it."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":363,"cache_read_input_tokens":154303,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":363,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01MTWvKbGnj3X7Sz2TpJ8d7a","session_id":"b566403e-4c11-4a9b-ad3a-d43b1f08afd2","uuid":"f38d9936-9613-48df-ad5d-353ea87ef6c6","timestamp":"2026-08-31T04:08:38.943Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Area 3 tests: sha3+xof"}
