2`, **`24`**, `SODIUM_SIZE_MAX` | [ ] |\n57\t| 5.39 | `crypto_stream_xsalsa20` | 24-byte `n` = all-`0x00`, all-`0xff`, pseudorandom; `clen` over **L** | [ ] |\n58\t| 5.40 | `crypto_stream_xsalsa20_xor` | out-of-place, pseudorandom `m`; `mlen` over **L** | [ ] |\n59\t| 5.41 | `crypto_stream_xsalsa20_xor` | in-place (`c == m`); round-trip; `mlen` over **L** | [ ] |\n60\t| 5.42 | `crypto_stream_xsalsa20_xor_ic` | `ic = 0`; must byte-equal `crypto_stream_xsalsa20_xor` (which is defined as `_xor_ic(..., 0ULL, ...)`); `mlen` over **L** | [ ] |\n61\t| 5.43 | `crypto_stream_xsalsa20_xor_ic` | `ic = 1` and small `ic ∈ {2, 3, 7}`; `mlen` over **L** | [ ] |\n62\t| 5.44 | `crypto_stream_xsalsa20_xor_ic` | `ic = 0xFFFFFFFF` (32-bit boundary) and `ic = 0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF` (64-bit rollover mid-message); `mlen ∈ {64, 65, 128, 129, 192}` | [ ] |\n63\t| 5.45 | `crypto_stream_xsalsa20` / `_xor_ic` vs `crypto_stream_salsa20*` | equivalence: `crypto_stream_xsalsa20(c, clen, n, k)` must equal `crypto_stream_salsa20(c, clen, n + 16, hsalsa20(n, k))`; same for `_xor_ic`; `clen ∈ {0, 64, 65, 512}` | [ ] |\n64\t| 5.46 | `crypto_stream_xsalsa20_keygen` | 32-byte output; length + non-constancy | [ ] |\n65\t| 5.47 | `crypto_stream_chacha20_keybytes`, `_noncebytes`, `_messagebytes_max` | no inputs; assert `32`, **`8`**, `SODIUM_SIZE_MAX` | [ ] |\n66\t| 5.48 | `crypto_stream_chacha20` (original, 8-byte nonce) | `k`/`n` = all-`0x00`; `clen` over **L**. Note the impl does `memset(c, 0, clen)` then encrypts in place. | [ ] |\n67\t| 5.49 | `crypto_stream_chacha20` | `k`/`n` = all-`0xff`, and DJB chacha20 test-vector `k`/`n`; `clen` over **L** | [ ] |\n68\t| 5.50 | `crypto_stream_chacha20_xor` | out-of-place, pseudorandom `m`; `mlen` over **L** (exercises `bytes < 64` `tmp[64]` zero-pad path for non-multiples, and the `bytes == 64` direct-exit path) | [ ] |\n69\t| 5.51 | `crypto_stream_chacha20_xor` | in-place (`c == m`); round-trip; `m` = all-zero equals `crypto_stream_chacha20`; `mlen` over **L** | 