{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_jir44ekwqpalpl66ftdhtu2upbuyqesxc2mxgde3fgeghw4matnq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_bdrk_01Bca4y2yzKyPh85uig2jCcg","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Area 7: kx/kdf/kem tests","run_in_background":true,"prompt":"Repo root: /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-RqaJY6 (call it $ROOT).\nC-to-Rust differential verification of libsodium 1.0.23. NARROW SCOPE: crypto_kx + crypto_kdf +\ncrypto_kem. (Other agents own a7_scalarmult.rs, a7_sign.rs and a7_box.rs — do NOT touch those.)\n\nWrite TWO test files, first one to green, then the second:\n1. `$ROOT/translation/tests/a7_kx_kdf.rs`\n2. `$ROOT/translation/tests/a7_kem.rs`\n\nC sources: c_src/libsodium/crypto_kx/crypto_kx.c;\nc_src/libsodium/crypto_kdf/{crypto_kdf.c,blake2b/kdf_blake2b.c,hkdf/kdf_hkdf_sha256.c,\nhkdf/kdf_hkdf_sha512.c}; c_src/libsodium/crypto_kem/{crypto_kem.c,mlkem768/kem_mlkem768.c,\nmlkem768/ref/kem_mlkem768_ref.c,xwing/kem_xwing.c}; headers crypto_kx.h, crypto_kdf*.h,\ncrypto_kem*.h. Run `nm -D` on `$ROOT/c_src/build/libsodium.so | grep -E 'crypto_kx|crypto_kdf|crypto_kem'`\nfirst to get the exact exported symbol list, and use the harness `has()` for anything unsure.\n\nWORK LIST: the crypto_kx, crypto_kdf and crypto_kem rows of\n`$ROOT/translation/phaseA/configs_7.md` and `$ROOT/translation/phaseA/errors_7.md`. READ THE\n\"global observations\" SECTION carefully — load-bearing subtleties include:\n- the crypto_kx ALIASING FOOTGUN: with `tx == NULL` the client's byte-interleaved loop\n  (`rx[i]=keys[i]; tx[i]=keys[i+32]`) leaves the caller's `rx` buffer holding the TX key; the\n  server has the reverse loop order. Both must be replicated exactly — test `rx == NULL`,\n  `tx == NULL`, and both non-NULL, and compare the full output buffers.\n- kx with BOTH `rx` and `tx` NULL calls `sodium_misuse()` (abort) — use `eq_abort`.\n- mlkem768 `_dec` NEVER returns -1 (implicit rejection via cmov of SHAKE256(z ‖ ct)); the only\n  reachable xwing decapsulation failure is a small-order `ct[1088..1119]`.\n- the seed-length contract mismatch: `crypto_kem_xwing_SEEDBYTES == 32` for `_seed_keypair` but\n  `_enc_deterministic` takes `seed[64]`; mlkem768 is the mirror image.\n- output-buffer-on-failure behaviour: pre-fill every output buffer with a known pattern and\n  compare C vs Rust byte for byte AFTER A FAILURE, not just the return code.\n\na7_kx_kdf.rs must cover: `crypto_kx_keypair`, `_seed_keypair`, `_client_session_keys`,\n`_server_session_keys` (all rx/tx NULL combinations, bad/all-zero/small-order public keys),\nall accessors; `crypto_kdf_derive_from_key` and `crypto_kdf_blake2b_derive_from_key` over\n`subkey_len` 0 / MIN-1 / MIN / typical / MAX / MAX+1, many `subkey_id` values (0, 1, 2^32,\nu64::MAX) and randomized 8-byte contexts; `crypto_kdf_keygen`; `crypto_kdf_primitive` and all\naccessors; hkdf-sha256 AND hkdf-sha512: `_extract`, `_expand` (out_len 0 / 1 / typical / MAX /\nMAX+1), `_extract_init`/`_extract_update`/`_extract_final` with 0, 1 and many randomized update\nchunks, `_keygen`, all accessors. For randomness-consuming calls use `rng_reset()` before each\nC/Rust pair.\n\na7_kem.rs must cover: for mlkem768 and xwing — `_keypair`, `_seed_keypair`, `_enc`, `_dec`,\n`_enc_deterministic` (if exported), full round trips, C↔Rust interop in both directions,\nciphertexts corrupted in many byte positions (asserting the implicit-rejection behaviour, i.e.\n`_dec` still returns 0 but yields a different shared secret), ciphertexts one byte short/long\nwhere the API allows it, all-zero and all-0xff keys/ciphertexts, the small-order\n`ct[1088..1119]` xwing rejection, plus the generic `crypto_kem_*` dispatch and every accessor.\n\nRULES (absolute):\n- `$ROOT/c_src/` is READ-ONLY ground truth. NEVER modify it. The C is ALWAYS correct.\n- Run cargo from `$ROOT/translation`, ALWAYS `--offline` (no network), always under `timeout`.\n- `cargo test --test X` does NOT rebuild the cdylib — run `timeout 900 cargo build --offline`\n  first every time. The harness hard-fails on a stale .so.\n- All calls go through `libloading` + `dlsym` on BOTH .so files — never call Rust directly.\n- Harness `$ROOT/translation/tests/common/mod.rs`: `both::<FnType>(\"sym\")`, `has(\"sym\")`,\n  `eqb`, `eqi`, `hex`, `Rng::new(seed)`, `padded`/`check_pad`, `rng_reset`/`rng_reseed`\n  (thread-local, safe under parallel tests), `errno`/`set_errno`, `eq_abort`.\n  Read `$ROOT/translation/tests/a7_scalarmult.rs` for the established style.\n- On divergence the C is right: fix `$ROOT/translation/src/*.rs` surgically (other agents are\n  editing other modules concurrently — touch only what you must, never reformat).\n\nFinish with both targets at 0 failures. Then tick ONLY the crypto_kx / crypto_kdf / crypto_kem\nrows of `configs_7.md` `[ ]` → `[x]` and append a status value (`verified` /\n`unreachable-from-public-API` / `undefined-behaviour-not-tested` / `not-exported`) to ONLY those\nrows of `errors_7.md` (add the ` | status |` header column and widen the separator row if not\nalready present; leave other rows' status cells empty for the other agents).\nReport: test counts, rows checked off, divergences found+fixed, gaps+reasons."}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6628,"cache_read_input_tokens":294406,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":6628,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b566403e-4c11-4a9b-ad3a-d43b1f08afd2","uuid":"c4edcd8a-3fc5-4332-9037-7851a633559b","timestamp":"2026-08-31T04:09:10.181Z"}
