kdf_derive_from_key` and `crypto_kdf_blake2b_derive_from_key` over\n`subkey_len` 0 / MIN-1 / MIN / typical / MAX / MAX+1, many `subkey_id` values (0, 1, 2^32,\nu64::MAX) and randomized 8-byte contexts; `crypto_kdf_keygen`; `crypto_kdf_primitive` and all\naccessors; hkdf-sha256 AND hkdf-sha512: `_extract`, `_expand` (out_len 0 / 1 / typical / MAX /\nMAX+1), `_extract_init`/`_extract_update`/`_extract_final` with 0, 1 and many randomized update\nchunks, `_keygen`, all accessors. For randomness-consuming calls use `rng_reset()` before each\nC/Rust pair.\n\na7_kem.rs must cover: for mlkem768 and xwing — `_keypair`, `_seed_keypair`, `_enc`, `_dec`,\n`_enc_deterministic` (if exported), full round trips, C↔Rust interop in both directions,\nciphertexts corrupted in many byte positions (asserting the implicit-rejection behaviour, i.e.\n`_dec` still returns 0 but yields a different shared secret), ciphertexts one byte short/long\nwhere the API allows it, all-zero and all-0xff keys/ciphertexts, the small-order\n`ct[1088..1119]` xwing rejection, plus the generic `crypto_kem_*` dispatch and every accessor.\n\nRULES (absolute):\n- `$ROOT/c_src/` is READ-ONLY ground truth. NEVER modify it. The C is ALWAYS correct.\n- Run cargo from `$ROOT/translation`, ALWAYS `--offline` (no network), always under `timeout`.\n- `cargo test --test X` does NOT rebuild the cdylib — run `timeout 900 cargo build --offline`\n  first every time. The harness hard-fails on a stale .so.\n- All calls go through `libloading` + `dlsym` on BOTH .so files — never call Rust directly.\n- Harness `$ROOT/translation/tests/common/mod.rs`: `both::<FnType>(\"sym\")`, `has(\"sym\")`,\n  `eqb`, `eqi`, `hex`, `Rng::new(seed)`, `padded`/`check_pad`, `rng_reset`/`rng_reseed`\n  (thread-local, safe under parallel tests), `errno`/`set_errno`, `eq_abort`.\n  Read `$ROOT/translation/tests/a7_scalarmult.rs` for the established style.\n- On divergence the C is right: fix `$ROOT/translation/src/*.rs` surgically (other agents are\n  editing other modules concurrently — touch only what you must, never reformat).\n\nFinish with both targets at 0 failures. Then tick ONLY the crypto_kx / crypto_kdf / crypto_kem\nrows of `configs_7.md` `[ ]` → `[x]` and append a status value (`verified` /\n`unreachable-from-public-API` / `undefined-behaviour-not-tested` / `not-exported`) to ONLY those\nrows of `errors_7.md` (add the ` | status |` header column and widen the separator row if not\nalready present; leave other rows' status cells empty for the other agents).\nReport: test counts, rows checked off, divergences found+fixed, gaps+reasons.","outputFile":"/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-agent-LlK7ZE/tmp/claude-31072124/-local-home-scheschb--harvest-work-harvest-work-RqaJY6/b566403e-4c11-4a9b-ad3a-d43b1f08afd2/tasks/afb78ca9809d09fb8.output","canReadOutputFile":true}}
