{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_dz6xbt7zdpflpcwd3gixz7e6xkykfbrbemjcqmjxfvdqvwsmsyxq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. Both test targets are green.\n\n## Test counts\n\n| target | tests | result |\n|---|---|---|\n| `translation/tests/a3_generichash.rs` | 38 | 0 failures (~17 s) |\n| `translation/tests/a3_shorthash.rs` | 14 | 0 failures |\n\nRun with `timeout 600 cargo test --offline --test a3_generichash --test a3_shorthash` from `$ROOT/translation`. Every call goes through `libloading`/`dlsym` on both `.so`s; `nm -D` showed **all 58** generichash/blake2b/shorthash symbols exported by both libraries, so nothing had to be skipped via `has()`.\n\n## Divergence found and fixed (1)\n\n`crypto_generichash_blake2b_final` — `$ROOT/translation/src/blake2b.rs:680`. The C has a *live* `assert(outlen <= UINT8_MAX)` (the CMake build sets no `CMAKE_BUILD_TYPE`, so no `-DNDEBUG`). The port omitted it, so `outlen == 257` truncated to `1` and returned `0` where C dies on `SIGABRT`. `outlen ∈ {0, 65..255, 256, 512, usize::MAX}` already aborted in both by other routes; only `outlen > 255` with a low byte in `1..=64` diverged. Fixed with a 3-line guard calling `crate::csys::abort()` (the convention already used in `core_ed25519.rs` / `ed25519_ref10_ristretto.rs`). No other file touched, nothing reformatted.\n\n## Coverage highlights\n\n- **Full opaque-state comparison** (384 bytes from `statebytes()`) after `init` and after **every** `update`, plus after `final` — used everywhere, including 1-byte-update runs over 1 KiB and randomized multi-chunk splits up to 9999 bytes. Also asserts nothing is written past `sizeof(blake2b_state)` (361).\n- `outlen` 0..66 × `keylen` 0..66 (4489 combos) for `crypto_generichash_blake2b`, `crypto_generichash`, `_salt_personal`, `_init`, `crypto_generichash_init`, `_init_salt_personal` — exact sentinel asserted per cell (`-1` only for `outlen==0`, `outlen>64`, `keylen>64`; `BYTES_MIN`/`KEYBYTES_MIN` confirmed **not** enforced), plus `65/66/128/255/256/257/4096/usize::MAX`.\n- The key-NULL asymmetry: one-shot **aborts** (`eq_abort`) for `key==NULL, 0<keylen<=64`, returns `-1` for `keylen>64`, while `_init`/`_init_salt_personal` silently do an unkeyed init (proved byte-identical to the `keylen==0` state, `buflen==0` vs `128` for keyed).\n- `final` with `outlen != init outlen`: all 10×10 size pairs asserted to be an exact prefix of the 64-byte digest of that state *and* different from a native-`outlen` init.\n- Double-`final` → `-1` with `out` and state untouched; triple-`final`; `update`-after-`final` → `0` then `-1`; re-`init` after `final` == fresh init.\n- `last_node`/`f[1]` proven inert; `_sodium_blake2b_init_param` fed 60+ arbitrary 64-byte param blocks; `_sodium_blake2b_compress_ref` driven over randomized `h/t/f/buf`; all low-level `sodium_misuse()` sites (rows 3.74–3.83) driven directly through the exported `_sodium_blake2b*` symbols.\n- Shorthash: an **independent SipHash-2-4 oracle** written from the spec inside the test (anchored on the reference vector `310e0edd47db6f72`) checks every digest, which turns the `inlen << 56` mod-256 length-byte aliasing into a real assertion (`oracle_len(msg,k,inlen) == oracle_len(msg,k,inlen&0xff)`) rather than a C-vs-Rust tautology. Lengths 0..=300 plus up to 65536, 6 key shapes, 5 content patterns, 3000-case fuzz, all 128 key-bit flips, message-bit flips, aliased `out`/`in`, and the two `siphashx24` halves checked separately.\n- Two known-answer anchors for BLAKE2b (empty message @512, `\"abc\"` @256) so a shared bug cannot pass.\n\n## Rows checked off\n\n`$ROOT/translation/phaseA/configs_3.md`: **44 rows** `3.84`–`3.127` flipped `[ ]` → `[x]`.\n`$ROOT/translation/phaseA/errors_3.md`: **74 rows** `3.34`–`3.107` given a status column value.\n\n## Gaps (and why)\n\n- `errors_3.md` rows marked `unreachable-from-public-API`, with the reason inline: 3.37 (dead `inlen > UINT64_MAX`), 3.40 (assert pre-empted by the range check), 3.54/3.72/3.85 (compile-time `COMPILER_ASSERT`; the 384-byte state size *is* verified at runtime via `statebytes()`), 3.61 (source note only), 3.65/3.73 (`memcpy` from/to NULL — UB, no defined C result to compare against), 3.71 (`buflen <= 128` invariant), 3.80/3.84 (`blake2b_init_param` can never return `< 0`).\n- `configs_3.md` rows **3.128–3.131** are area-wide (they also cover sha2/sha3/xof) and were deliberately left unticked for whichever agent finishes the area; their generichash/shorthash content is nonetheless exercised (content patterns 0x00/0xff/`i&0xff`/random, state reuse, aliased buffers, primitive-vs-generic equivalence).\n- Rows `3.1`–`3.33` of both files belong to the sha2/sha3/xof agents; I did not touch them. I also did not re-run `build-phaseA.sh` (it regenerates the shared `ERRORS.md`/`CONFIGS.md` from all eight fragments and other agents are still editing theirs)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":590,"cache_read_input_tokens":187321,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":590,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_019esovLKbek6PhVhz8MDC6r","session_id":"b566403e-4c11-4a9b-ad3a-d43b1f08afd2","uuid":"55e2fc24-0b01-4b5a-ac92-9a19fa114c69","timestamp":"2026-08-31T04:14:48.977Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Area 3 tests: generichash+shorthash"}
