 each C/Rust pair),\n  `crypto_kx_client_session_keys`, `crypto_kx_server_session_keys` across all rx/tx NULL\n  combinations, with valid, all-zero, all-0xff and small-order peer public keys; a full\n  client/server agreement round trip (client rx == server tx and vice versa); every accessor\n  (`_publickeybytes`, `_secretkeybytes`, `_seedbytes`, `_sessionkeybytes`, `_primitive`).\n- `crypto_kdf_derive_from_key` and `crypto_kdf_blake2b_derive_from_key` over `subkey_len`\n  0 / MIN-1 / MIN / several typical / MAX / MAX+1, `subkey_id` values 0, 1, 255, 2^32,\n  u64::MAX and randomized ones, randomized 8-byte contexts including all-zero and all-0xff,\n  and randomized 32-byte keys. Assert the EXACT sentinel for every rejected combination.\n- `crypto_kdf_keygen`, `crypto_kdf_primitive`, and every kdf accessor.\n- hkdf-sha256 AND hkdf-sha512: `_extract`, `_expand` (out_len 0 / 1 / several typical / MAX /\n  MAX+1), `_extract_init` / `_extract_update` / `_extract_final` with 0, 1 and many randomized\n  update chunks (compare the FULL opaque state bytes between C and Rust after init and after\n  every update, sized with the `*_statebytes()` accessor if one exists), `_keygen`, and every\n  accessor. Also assert `extract_init/update/final` equals the one-shot `_extract` for the same\n  input, in both libraries.\n- Use MANY randomized inputs per row with fixed seeds; use `padded`/`check_pad` on every output\n  buffer.\n\nRULES (absolute):\n- `$ROOT/c_src/` is READ-ONLY ground truth. NEVER modify it. The C is ALWAYS correct.\n- Run cargo from `$ROOT/translation`, ALWAYS `--offline` (no network), always under `timeout`.\n- `cargo test --test X` does NOT rebuild the cdylib — run `timeout 900 cargo build --offline`\n  first every time. The harness hard-fails on a stale .so.\n- All calls go through `libloading` + `dlsym` on BOTH .so files — never call Rust directly.\n- Harness `$ROOT/translation/tests/common/mod.rs`: `both::<FnType>(\"sym\")`, `has(\"sym\")`,\n  `eqb`, `eqi`, `hex`, `Rng::new(seed)`, `padded`/`check_pad`, `rng_reset`/`rng_reseed`\n  (thread-local, safe under parallel tests), `errno`/`set_errno`, `eq_abort`.\n  Read `$ROOT/translation/tests/a7_scalarmult.rs` for the established style.\n- On divergence the C is right: fix `$ROOT/translation/src/*.rs` surgically (other agents are\n  editing other modules concurrently — touch only what you must, never reformat).\n\nFinish with `timeout 600 cargo test --offline --test a7_kx_kdf` at 0 failures. Then tick ONLY\nthe crypto_kx and crypto_kdf rows of `configs_7.md` `[ ]` → `[x]`, and append a status value\n(`verified` / `unreachable-from-public-API` / `undefined-behaviour-not-tested` / `not-exported`)\nto ONLY those rows of `errors_7.md`. If the ` | status |` header column is not present yet, add\nit and widen the separator row (match `$ROOT/translation/phaseA/errors_1.md`); leave other\nrows' status cells empty for the other agents.\nReport: test count, rows checked off, divergences found+fixed, gaps+reasons.","uuid":"964f274c-17c9-4985-90c2-64b8ba2dba46","session_id":"b566403e-4c11-4a9b-ad3a-d43b1f08afd2"}
