{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_fszmcyxjbmj6mjnn6g2it6pudnqfowcruzy53n2wamr4egfshjqq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. Area 2 bookkeeping is complete and everything is green.\n\n## 1. Existing suite verified\n`cargo build --offline` then the four named test binaries: **54 tests, 0 failures** (`a2_verify_core` 20, `a2_salsa_keccak` 6, `a2_ed25519` 18, `a2_ristretto255` 10).\n\n## 2. Audit result — real gaps found\nAll 128 config rows and 52 error rows map onto existing tests, **except** a set of rows that ask for *both arms* of a branch inside a `static`, non-exported helper of `ed25519_ref10.c`. Those were only covered probabilistically (\"a random sweep should hit both ~50% of the time\") or, for the folded ristretto rejections, not distinguishable at all. Rows affected: configs 2.94, 2.95, 2.96, 2.103, 2.112/2.113, 2.114; errors 2.12/2.14/2.15/2.16/2.17, 2.39, 2.42/2.43.\n\n## 3. Tests added — `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-RqaJY6/translation/tests/a2_gaps.rs` (9 tests)\nCarries a **test-side** `F_p` (`p = 2^255-19`) implementation plus statement-by-statement replicas of `ge25519_elligator2`, `ge25519_mont_to_ed`, `fe25519_reduce64`, `ristretto255_sqrt_ratio_m1`, `_is_canonical`, `_frombytes`, `_p3_tobytes`, `_elligator`. Each replica is **validated end-to-end against the C library** through exported entry points (`_sodium_ge25519_from_uniform`/`_from_hash`/`_clear_cofactor`/`_p3_tobytes`/`_p3_add`, `_sodium_ristretto255_frombytes`/`_p3_tobytes`, `crypto_core_ristretto255_from_hash`, `_sodium_fe25519_invert`), so a mis-classification fails the test instead of producing a false tick. It then *classifies* inputs and asserts every arm is non-empty. Highlights:\n\n- `elligator2_both_notsquare_arms` — asserts >50 square and >50 non-square `gx1` inputs, both `x_sign` values, and both outcomes of the `x_sign` cmov.\n- `mont_to_ed_cmov_path_at_zero` — proves row 2.96 is reachable from **exactly one input, `r == 0`**: `1+2r²=0` is unsolvable (`-1/2` is a non-residue), `y=0` with `x≠0` needs `A²-4` square (it isn't), and `x=0` needs `x1=-A` i.e. `r=0`, where `-A` is a non-residue so the `notsquare` arm is taken. Output must be the identity encoding.\n- `ristretto255_frombytes_every_rejection_arm` — separates the four folded `-1` reasons and requires each of non-canonical / `sqrt_ratio_m1==0` / `isnegative(T)` / `iszero(Y)` to fire at least once, while matching the library's return code *and* all four decoded `p3` coordinates.\n- `ristretto255_p3_tobytes_both_rotate_arms`, `ristretto255_elligator_both_square_arms`, `from_hash_reduce64_and_notsquare_arms`.\n- `scalar_random_redraw_loop` — replays the harness xorshift stream, predicts which candidate `crypto_core_ed25519_scalar_random` accepts, and requires both the first-draw-accepted and the re-draw cases to occur (error row 2.39 was previously untestable).\n- `core_h2c_h_len_assert_is_live` — checks `h_len > 0xff` dies on a **fatal signal** on both libraries and `h_len <= 0xff` does not, which also proves `NDEBUG` is absent (`eq_abort` alone would have passed even if the assert were compiled out).\n\nTotal now **63 tests, 0 failures** across the five `a2_*` binaries.\n\n## 4. Divergences\n**None between C and Rust.** No file under `translation/src/` was touched (and `c_src/` is untouched). The only bug found was in my own test-side replica: I initially encoded field elements as raw unsigned 26/25-bit limbs (the shape `fe25519_frombytes` emits), which is ~2× the bound `fe25519_sq`/`_mul` document once a value passes through one `fe25519_add` — e.g. inside `ge25519_p2_dbl` — so `clear_cofactor` silently produced wrong results. Fixed by emitting the *balanced* representation (`|l[even]| ≤ 2^25`, `|l[odd]| ≤ 2^24`) that the C code's own arithmetic produces.\n\n## 5. Bookkeeping\n- `phaseA/configs_2.md`: **all 128 rows ticked `[x]`**, plus a short notes section recording two factual corrections found while auditing: rows 2.94/2.103 say \"bit 5\" but `((r[31] >> 5) ^ optblocker_u8) >> 2` is `r[31] >> 7`, i.e. **bit 7** drives the branch (the split exists only to XOR in the `volatile` blocker); and the reachability analysis for row 2.96.\n- `phaseA/errors_2.md`: header widened to `| ... | status |` matching `errors_1.md` style; all 52 rows given a status — **48 `verified`**, **4 `unreachable-from-public-API`**: 2.10 (`fe25519_sqrt`; static, sole caller's failure path is the unreachable `abort()` of 2.40), 2.31 (`_string_to_points(n>2)`; both call sites pass literal 1/2), 2.35 (`from_string`'s tail `add`; `ge25519_from_hash` always emits a decodable on-curve point — asserted by the replica), 2.40 (`elligator2`'s `abort()`; the replica's `assert!(ok, …)` asserts it never triggers). A \"Phase-C status notes\" section explains each, and why 2.42/2.43 are `verified` rather than unreachable (the function *is* exported as `_sodium_core_h2c_string_to_hash`).\n- `./build-phaseA.sh` re-run: `wrote ERRORS.md (1153 lines) and CONFIGS.md (1542 lines)`; CONFIGS row-count table now shows `| 2 | 128 | 128 |`."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":705,"cache_read_input_tokens":254573,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":705,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01Y8KmEUWZuyfELGp9tb2pNF","session_id":"b566403e-4c11-4a9b-ad3a-d43b1f08afd2","uuid":"f9b4b444-f8a1-4ba4-a845-b71e3f18381a","timestamp":"2026-08-31T04:28:35.144Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Finish area 2 bookkeeping+gaps"}
