{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_52yhtdw7yq76qbd3yeqqgzkryclxuk3gu6jannkekuvhlf46opza","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. `timeout 600 cargo test --offline --test a7_kem` → **30 passed, 0 failed** (1.6 s).\n\n## What was written\n\n`/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-RqaJY6/translation/tests/a7_kem.rs` — 30 `#[test]` functions, all calls through `libloading`/`dlsym` on both `.so` files. Symbol list confirmed first: all **30** exported `crypto_kem*` symbols exist in C **and** Rust (full parity, nothing needed `has()` gating; `kem_symbol_surface` asserts all 30 plus the absence of an invented `crypto_kem_enc_deterministic`).\n\nCoverage highlights:\n- **Accessors/dispatch**: all 15 `*bytes` accessors against literal header values, `crypto_kem_primitive() == \"xwing\"` with pointer stability, `1120 == 1088+32`, `1216 == 1184+32`.\n- **Structural re-derivation from independent C primitives** (not just C-vs-Rust equality): ML-KEM `sk = skpv‖pk‖SHA3-256(pk)‖z`; X-Wing `expand_decaps_key` = `SHAKE256(seed,96)` split 64/32 with `pk[1184..] == base(sk_x)`; X-Wing `ct` split and the full combiner `SHA3-256(ss_mlkem‖ss_x‖ct_x‖pk_x‖5c2e2f2f5e5c)`.\n- **Implicit rejection**: every corrupted-ciphertext case asserts `rc == 0` (never `-1`), `ss != ss_enc`, C `ss` == Rust `ss`, **and** `ss == SHAKE256(z‖ct)` computed independently — plus the same through the X-Wing combiner. Dense sweeps: every 7th byte of the 1088-byte ML-KEM ct, whole-byte substitutions, zeroed regions, all 8 bits of both end bytes, all 256 bit-flips of the X-Wing X25519 half.\n- **X-Wing small-order rejection**: 10 encodings (the 7 blocklist entries + 3 high-bit variants) in `ct[1088..1120]` → exact `-1`, `ss` byte-identical to the prefill; contrasted with `p+2` (non-canonical but not blocklisted) → `0`.\n- **The one real validity check**: 13 coefficient positions × 3 non-canonical values → `-1` with `ct`/`ss` untouched, plus the 3328 canonical boundary accepted, all-0xff `pk` rejected, all-zero `pk` **accepted**; propagated through `_enc`, `xwing_enc*` and `crypto_kem_enc`.\n- **Interop both directions**: 4 combinations of {C,Rust} keygen × encap × decap for both KEMs.\n- 100 randomized round trips each for mlkem768 and xwing, 24 randomized keypairs each with `rng_reseed` before every pair, all-zero/all-0xff keys/ciphertexts/seeds, `padded`/`check_pad` on every output buffer.\n- **Seed-length contract**: mlkem `_enc_deterministic` proven to consume exactly 32 of the 64 `SEEDBYTES`; xwing `_enc_deterministic` proven to consume all 64 while `SEEDBYTES == 32`, including which bits survive X25519 clamping.\n\n## Rows checked off\n- `configs_7.md`: **16** rows ticked, 7.113–7.128 (7.129 kx/box and 7.130 build-config left for other agents).\n- `errors_7.md`: added the ` status |` header column + widened separator (was absent), annotated **17** rows, 7.110–7.126. 7.120 → `unreachable-from-public-API` (dead `mlkem768_dec != 0` branch); 7.126 → `undefined-behaviour-not-tested` (the trigger is a short-buffer OOB read — untestable; the *observable* half of that row, which bytes each entry point actually consumes, **is** verified by two dedicated tests); the other 15 → `verified`. 7.127/7.129 left blank (shared with other agents).\n\n## Divergences\n**None.** Zero edits to `translation/src/*.rs` were needed — the Rust `crypto_kem` translation is byte-exact against the C for every case above. The two initial test failures were my own wrong expectations, both corrected in the test (and both are genuine C behaviours worth recording): corrupting `z` at `sk[2368..2400]` is a **no-op for a valid ciphertext** (`z` is only consulted on the rejection path — now tested both ways), and the X-Wing ephemeral scalar `seed[32..64]` is **clamped**, so flipping the low 3 bits of `seed[32]` or bits 6/7 of `seed[63]` leaves `ct` and `ss` bit-identical.\n\n## Gaps\n- **Official FIPS 203 / X-Wing draft KAT vectors** (configs 7.113/7.115/7.120/7.122/7.124) are not embedded — no network access to fetch them. Substituted with something stronger for differential purposes: full structural re-derivation of every output from independent primitives (SHAKE256, SHA3-256, curve25519) plus determinism and cross-seed distinctness. This pins the C↔Rust equivalence but not conformance to the published vectors.\n- **NULL-pointer paths** (errors 7.129) not tested — UB by contract, and that row is shared with other agents.\n- `errors_7.md` 7.120's dead branch cannot be reached from the public API, as the row itself states."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":417,"cache_read_input_tokens":147660,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":417,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01ReaZahBvT4axs61k1onDcY","session_id":"b566403e-4c11-4a9b-ad3a-d43b1f08afd2","uuid":"eb61b30d-1e65-412a-baa3-f8e673df5d3b","timestamp":"2026-08-31T04:30:10.422Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Area 7: kem tests"}
