{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_s7jbreaak3oepeg5mq6qhjj27ozdzgkcsrs6xu6m2bvi2eg7pckq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done.\n\n## Result\n\n`timeout 600 cargo test --offline --test a7_kx_kdf` → **23 tests, 0 failures** (1.4 s).\n\nNew file: `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-RqaJY6/translation/tests/a7_kx_kdf.rs` (~1050 lines). Every call goes through `dlsym` on both `.so` files; every output buffer is `padded()`/`check_pad()`ed and pre-filled with a distinctive pattern so \"untouched on failure\" and \"no write past the requested length\" are compared byte for byte, not just by return code.\n\n### Exported-symbol list\n`nm -D` confirmed all 41 `crypto_kx_*` / `crypto_kdf_*` symbols; all 41 are exported by the Rust `.so` too (asserted in `kx_kdf_symbols_all_exported`, which also asserts that `crypto_kdf_statebytes` / `crypto_kdf_blake2b_statebytes` do *not* exist). Nothing needed `has()` gating except the auxiliary `crypto_auth_hmacsha*_{init,update,final,statebytes}` used as an independent oracle.\n\n### Rows checked off\n- `configs_7.md`: **7.81–7.112** (32 rows) `[ ]` → `[x]`.\n- `errors_7.md`: **7.92–7.109** (18 rows) → `verified`. The ` | status |` header column had already been added by another agent, so I only appended cells to my own rows; 7.127/7.129 (area-wide accessor/NULL rows) left empty for the other agents, as was 7.129 in `configs_7.md` (needs `crypto_box_beforenm`).\n\n### Divergences found: **0**\nThe Rust translations of `kx.rs` and `kdf.rs` are byte-faithful to the C, including the aliasing footgun, the `errno = EINVAL` sentinels and the `sodium_memzero` of the hkdf state. No `src/*.rs` edits were needed.\n\nTo prove the suite is not vacuous I ran a **negative control**: temporarily swapping the two store statements in `crypto_kx_server_session_keys` (a mutation invisible when `rx != tx`) made `kx_session_keys_null_and_aliased_outputs` and `kx_session_keys_bad_peer_public_key` fail immediately. `src/kx.rs` was restored and re-verified identical to `crypto_kx.c:107-108`.\n\n### Coverage highlights\n- **kx aliasing footgun**: for both roles × `{rx==NULL, tx==NULL, rx==tx, both distinct}`, asserted the *full* 32-byte buffers. Confirmed the client with `tx == NULL` leaves the caller's `rx` holding `keys[32..64]` — the **TX** key (`assert_ne!` against the real rx key) — and that the server's reversed loop leaves the surviving buffer holding the server's **RX** key. The unused buffer is asserted still to carry the prefill pattern.\n- **kx both-NULL** → `eq_abort` (both libraries `sig:6`).\n- **kx failure buffers**: 7 blocklist encodings + their high-bit variants + all-zero → `-1` with both buffers untouched, in all four NULL patterns. Note all-`0xff` is **not** blocklisted (it reduces to a valid x-coordinate) and legitimately returns 0 in both libraries.\n- **kdf blake2b**: `subkey_len` 0–15, 16–64 (all 49), 65, 100, 1000, `usize::MAX/2`, `usize::MAX-1`, `usize::MAX`; exact `EINVAL` asserted on every rejection, `subkey` untouched; generic alias byte-identical at every length; no shorter subkey is a prefix of a longer one. 41 `subkey_id`s (0, 1, 2, 255, 2^32-1, 2^32, 2^63, u64::MAX + 32 random), 35 contexts (all-zero, all-`0xff`, + random), 50 keys, plus a 256-case fully-randomised 4-axis sweep.\n- **hkdf**: RFC 5869 cases 1 and 3 pin the absolute values; 195-combo salt_len × ikm_len matrix per algorithm; the **full opaque state** (208 B / 416 B, via `*_statebytes()`, in an 8-byte-aligned guarded buffer) is compared after `init`, after *every* `update`, and after `final` (where both are asserted all-zero); streaming == one-shot asserted both transitively and explicitly **within each library separately** (128 more randomised cases with 0–9 chunks). `expand` out_len 0…BYTES_MAX and MAX+1/MAX+2/2×MAX/`usize::MAX` → `EINVAL` + untouched buffer; counter exhaustion at `out_len == BYTES_MAX` cross-checked against an independent `HMAC(prk, T(254)‖ctx‖255)` built from the public `crypto_auth_hmacsha*` API.\n\n### Gaps\n- `errors_7.md` 7.129 (NULL for `__attribute__((nonnull))` params such as `key`/`ctx` in `crypto_kdf*`): undefined behaviour, deliberately not exercised. The one row of defined NULL behaviour in my scope (`rx`/`tx`) is fully covered.\n- `configs_7.md` 7.129 (kx vs `crypto_box_beforenm` cross-area consistency) left unticked — it needs `crypto_box`, owned by another agent.\n- No published third-party vector exists for `crypto_kdf_blake2b_derive_from_key` or HKDF-SHA512, so those rows rest on C-vs-Rust equality plus structural properties (uniqueness across all four axes, non-prefix, prefix-extension of `expand`); HKDF-SHA256 is additionally pinned to RFC 5869."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":331,"cache_read_input_tokens":147662,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":331,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01LMyZ1bbwTduiEY9VxtpkU9","session_id":"b566403e-4c11-4a9b-ad3a-d43b1f08afd2","uuid":"5a78e24b-2deb-427d-b905-eca4b795d674","timestamp":"2026-08-31T04:31:11.786Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Area 7: kx+kdf tests"}
