{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_f4o4ya3yx2bwv4ywqqqde5nm3xynm3rieelcinmnx5rzpxz24woq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All three area-7 targets green. Final state confirmed.\n\n## Report\n\n### Files written\n- `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-RqaJY6/translation/tests/a7_sign.rs` — 19 test fns, all passing\n- `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-RqaJY6/translation/tests/a7_box.rs` — 14 test fns, all passing\n\n`a7_scalarmult.rs` re-run to confirm no collateral damage: 23 passed. `src/*.rs` and `c_src/` untouched.\n\n```\na7_sign        19 passed; 0 failed\na7_box         14 passed; 0 failed\na7_scalarmult  23 passed; 0 failed   (pre-existing, unchanged)\n```\n\n### Divergences found and fixed\n**None.** Zero `src/*.rs` edits were required — the sign and box translations matched C byte for byte on every input, including all error paths and post-failure buffer contents. (Verified the tests are real: `LD_DEBUG=bindings` confirms `liblibsodium.so` binds `crypto_secretbox_detached`/`crypto_core_hsalsa20` to *itself*, not to the C `.so`; and the RFC 8032 KATs plus a deliberately-wrong assertion I hit mid-development both exercised the Rust side.)\n\n### Coverage highlights\n**sign**: RFC 8032 §7.1 KATs 1–3; message lengths **every value 0..=300** plus 1023/1024/1025/2048/4096/8191/8192/8193/16384/65536; `_keypair`/`_seed_keypair` (with `rng_reseed` per pair) incl. all-zero/all-`0xff`/`L` seeds; `_sk_to_seed`/`_sk_to_pk` incl. three overlapping-buffer aliasings; attached + in-place `m == sm+64` and `m == sm`; `open` with `smlen ∈ 0..64`, every byte of `sm` flipped × 2 bit masks × 11 lengths (proving the `memset(m,0,mlen)` on the bad-sig path vs. *untouched* on the short path); `verify_detached` with all 64 sig byte positions × 3 masks × 7 lengths; non-canonical `S` (`S+L`, `S=L`, `S=L-1`, forced high/low nibble, `0`, `ff..ff`); non-canonical `R`/`pk` (all 38 encodings); all 8 small-order encodings as both `A` and `R`; multipart with 0/1/many updates, 10 fixed splits + 24 randomized splits over 1024 bytes (streaming invariance), cross-chunked verify, DOM2PREFIX cross-domain rejection both ways; `_crypto_sign_ed25519_{detached,verify_detached}` with `prehashed ∈ {0,1}` and `_ref10_hinit` state/digest comparison; `pk_to_curve25519`/`sk_to_curve25519` consistency + the sign→box bridge; C↔Rust interop in both directions for detached and attached.\n\n**Cofactoring (the load-bearing subtlety)**: constructed a genuinely off-main-subgroup key `A' = A + T` (order 8L) and signed with the doctored `sk' = seed ‖ A'` — since `_detached` takes the hashed public key from `sk[32..64]`, the verifier's `check` is `h·T`, small-order but non-identity. C **accepts** (`0`), Rust matches; the same signature fails under the honest `pk`; and `pk_to_curve25519(A')` returns `-1` — the exact `is_on_main_subgroup` vs. canonicality asymmetry.\n\n**box**: both primitives × `_easy`/`_open_easy`, `_detached`/`_open_detached`, `_beforenm` + all four `*_afternm`, `_seal`/`_seal_open`, plus the xsalsa-only NaCl padded `crypto_box`/`_open`/`_afternm`/`_open_afternm` and the generic wrappers (asserted bit-identical to the explicit xsalsa names). Lengths **every value 0..=300** plus up to 131073 (crosses `STREAM_POLY1305_CHUNK`); `clen ∈ 0..16`, `=16`, `=17`; `clen == 0` legal for `*_open_detached*`; tag+body corrupted at **every** byte position for `open_easy`, `open_easy_afternm`, `open_detached`, `open_detached_afternm`; all 7 blocklisted small-order pks (± bit 255) on every entry point with post-failure buffer comparison; seal reconstructed from its parts (`epk = base(randombytes_buf)`, nonce = `BLAKE2b-24(epk‖pk)`, body = `_easy`); `_seal` with a small-order recipient proved to still `memcpy` `c[0..32]` while leaving `c[32..]` untouched; all 6 `sodium_misuse()` `mlen` guards checked via `eq_abort` (both abort with SIGABRT); C↔Rust interop both directions for easy/detached/seal/padded.\n\n### Rows checked off\n- `configs_7.md`: **52 rows** ticked `[ ]` → `[x]` — `7.29`–`7.59` (crypto_sign) and `7.60`–`7.80` (crypto_box). No other rows touched.\n- `errors_7.md`: **58 rows** annotated with a status cell — `7.34`–`7.58` (sign) and `7.59`–`7.91` (box). The `| status |` header column and widened separator were already present. Statuses: `verified` for 53 rows; `unreachable-from-public-API` for `7.35`, `7.52`, `7.56`, `7.78`; `verified / unreachable-from-public-API` for `7.89` (misuse half reachable, keypair-failure half dead).\n\n### Gaps and reasons\n1. **`7.35`** (`smlen - 64 > MESSAGEBYTES_MAX`) — arithmetically impossible on LP64; dead branch, structurally present in Rust.\n2. **`7.52`, `7.78`, `7.89`-part** — `_crypto_sign_ed25519_detached` and `crypto_box*_keypair` have no failure path, so their `LCOV_EXCL` error branches are unreachable.\n3. **`7.56`** — the *absence* of `ge25519_is_canonical` in `pk_to_curve25519` is structurally real but **not observable**: every non-canonical encoding reduces to `y ∈ [0,19)`, none of which is a non-small-order main-subgroup point. All 38 candidates (19 `y` × ±bit 255) are rejected by both libraries; a permanent assertion pins `pk2c_accepted == 0`.\n4. **NULL pointers** other than the explicitly NULL-checked `siglen_p`/`smlen_p`/`mlen_p`/`m` are `__attribute__((nonnull))` → UB, not tested.\n5. **`mlen == MESSAGEBYTES_MAX`** (just under the misuse guard) needs a 2^64-byte buffer; only the boundary arithmetic is asserted via the accessor.\n6. RFC 8032's 1023-byte KAT is not embedded (I did not want to risk a mistyped 2046-char vector); that length is covered differentially, with KATs 1–3 as correctness anchors.\n\n### Three discrepancies in the phase-A notes (tests assert the *real* C behaviour, notes left unedited)\n- `errors_7.md` **7.66/7.67/7.68** claim `m` is zeroed over `clen`/`clen-16` on MAC failure. It is not: `crypto_secretbox_open_detached` returns `-1` *before* touching `m` (`crypto_secretbox_easy.c:126-129`). Tests assert the buffer is left with its prefill pattern in both libraries.\n- `errors_7.md` **7.69** says the NaCl `crypto_box_open` guard is `clen < BOXZEROBYTES (16)`. The actual guard is `clen < 32` in `crypto_secretbox_xsalsa20poly1305_open`. Tested over `clen ∈ 0..40`.\n- `configs_7.md` **7.46** posits a genuine signature with `(sig[63] & 240) != 0`. Since `S < L ≈ 2^252`, that never happens (0/64 sampled signatures); the non-short-circuit branch is instead exercised with crafted *canonical* `S ∈ [2^252, L)` (`L-1`, `L-2`, `2^252`, `2^252+k`), which pass `sc25519_is_canonical` and then fail the group equation."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":809,"cache_read_input_tokens":270763,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":809,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01Uv4zSn6cVxw3q2P7zcvEiR","session_id":"b566403e-4c11-4a9b-ad3a-d43b1f08afd2","uuid":"f55cbc84-c9d7-40ea-8f26-e398a7b42171","timestamp":"2026-08-31T04:34:09.942Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Area 7: sign + box tests"}
