{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_anli7dzclupkfuq3vxw7k3zkh7gmzo5jq4m73bdfui5s32xt5lja","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Everything is green. Final state:\n\n## Files created\n\n| file | tests | rows covered |\n|---|---|---|\n| `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-RqaJY6/translation/tests/a8_argon2.rs` | 17 | configs 8.1–8.36, errors 8.1–8.52 |\n| `.../tests/a8_argon2_core.rs` | 19 | configs 8.37–8.75, 8.87–8.90; errors 8.53–8.111, 8.148 |\n| `.../tests/a8_argon2_encoding.rs` | 7 | configs 8.76–8.86; errors 8.112–8.147 |\n| `.../tests/a8_scrypt.rs` | 19 | configs 8.91–8.122; errors 8.149–8.201 |\n| `.../tests/a8_ipcrypt.rs` | 10 | configs 8.123–8.150; errors 8.202–8.214 |\n\n**72 tests, 0 failures** (`timeout 600 cargo test --offline --test <name>` for each; also verified in a full-suite run — no failures anywhere). Slowest: `a8_scrypt` 18.8 s (dominated by the single 1 GiB SENSITIVE-preset test `r8_108`), `a8_argon2` 4.1 s.\n\nWorklists updated: **all 150 rows of `configs_8.md` checked off**; **all 214 rows of `errors_8.md` annotated** — 162 `verified`, 52 `unreachable-from-public-API` (each with the concrete reason appended).\n\n## Divergences found and fixed (1 real bug, in `src/argon2_encoding.rs`)\n\n`_sodium_argon2_decode_string` and `_sodium_argon2_encode_string` declared their `type` parameter as the Rust 2-variant `#[repr(C)] enum argon2_type` and dispatched with an exhaustive `match`. An external caller passing anything other than 1/2 (legal in C — the parameter is an `int`) produced an invalid discriminant and the wrong arm was taken:\n\n- `argon2_decode_string(ctx, \"$argon2id$…\", 0)` returned `ARGON2_OK` (0); C returns `ARGON2_INCORRECT_TYPE` (**-26**)\n- `argon2_encode_string(dst, len, ctx, 0)` returned 0; C returns `ARGON2_ENCODING_FAIL` (**-31**)\n\nFix: both functions now take `c_int` and compare numerically with an explicit `else` mirroring the C `default:`. To avoid ever materialising an invalid enum value, the plain-`int` type was propagated through the FFI boundary of `_sodium_argon2_ctx`, `_sodium_argon2_hash`, `_sodium_argon2_verify` (which only forward the value; `argon2_ctx` narrows to the enum *after* its `INCORRECT_TYPE` check) and the two `extern` declarations in `src/argon2.rs` / `src/pwhash_argon2.rs`. No other Rust source was touched.\n\n## Spec errors in the Phase A tables (C is authoritative) — documented in the .md files\n\n- **errors 8.148**: `sodium_bin2base64` does **not** return NULL on a short buffer — it calls `sodium_misuse()` and aborts. So `argon2_encode_string`/`argon2_hash` abort (not `-31`) as soon as `dst_len` is big enough to clear the last `SS` (≥27 for `$argon2i$v=19$m=8,t=1,p=1$`; 61 is the tightest accepting size for saltlen 8/hashlen 16). Verified with `eq_abort`.\n- **errors 8.48**: first rejected `memlimit` is `4398046511104`, not `>4398046511104`.\n- **errors 8.116**: `\"v=1a9\"` → `-26`, not `-32` (the version check precedes the next `CC`).\n- **errors 8.133**: `\"…$YWJjZA==\"` → `-2`, not `-32` (validation runs before the trailing-NUL check).\n- **errors 8.139**: a trailing `'x'` is valid Base64 and just lengthens the digest; real garbage needs a non-alphabet char.\n- **errors 8.183–8.185**: `decode64_one` is `strchr(itoa64, c)`, which matches `itoa64`'s own NUL and yields 64, so a short `$7$` setting reads past its terminator and a truncation landing on the last char of the `r`/`p` field still parses. Tests use fixed-size, fully-determined setting buffers.\n- **configs 8.35**: the row's literal `m=8,t=1,p=2` string is rejected (`m < 8*lanes` → `-14`), so `needs_rehash` returns `-1`; the \"`p` is not compared\" quirk is pinned with `m=16,t=1,p=2` instead.\n- **configs 8.17/8.44/8.45**: `m_cost` 8/9/10/11 give *different digests* (`argon2_initial_hash` hashes the raw `m_cost`); only the work is identical.\n\n## Not covered, with reasons\n\n- **Not exported by either `.so`**: `argon2_encodedlen`, `argon2_error_message` — so no differential comparison of error strings was possible. (Symbol sets of the two libraries are otherwise byte-identical: `comm -3` over `nm -D` yields 0 lines.)\n- **errors 8.7 / 8.18 / 8.149** (`outlen > BYTES_MAX`): `memset(out, 0, outlen)` runs *before* the check, so exercising them needs a >4 GiB (argon2) / >137 GB (scrypt) caller buffer.\n- **errors 8.106 / 8.181** (mmap failure): would `mmap(MAP_POPULATE)` 4 TiB / 256 GiB. `escrypt_alloc_region` failure *is* covered safely with a 2^62-byte request (row 8.198).\n- **errors 8.155**: `pickparams` can never produce `r*p >= 2^30`; any other inner `_ll` failure needs a ≥64 GiB region.\n- The remaining 48 unreachable rows are genuine dead C branches on this platform (field already `uint32_t`, minimum of 0, `pickparams`/`escrypt_init_local` never failing, non-mmap fallback not compiled, dead enum values).\n\nOne incidental note: `tests/a1_randombytes_impl.rs` (area 1, not mine) failed once during a full-suite run while the shared cdylib was being rebuilt concurrently; it passes 5/5 in isolation and in later full runs."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":845,"cache_read_input_tokens":438105,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":845,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_013PupbdJbvdcm1hFvbZnzS8","session_id":"b566403e-4c11-4a9b-ad3a-d43b1f08afd2","uuid":"74d5de0d-7546-479b-8576-6aafddfd454c","timestamp":"2026-08-31T04:51:10.606Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Phase B/C tests area 8"}
