ve *different digests* (`argon2_initial_hash` hashes the raw `m_cost`); only the work is identical.\n\n## Not covered, with reasons\n\n- **Not exported by either `.so`**: `argon2_encodedlen`, `argon2_error_message` — so no differential comparison of error strings was possible. (Symbol sets of the two libraries are otherwise byte-identical: `comm -3` over `nm -D` yields 0 lines.)\n- **errors 8.7 / 8.18 / 8.149** (`outlen > BYTES_MAX`): `memset(out, 0, outlen)` runs *before* the check, so exercising them needs a >4 GiB (argon2) / >137 GB (scrypt) caller buffer.\n- **errors 8.106 / 8.181** (mmap failure): would `mmap(MAP_POPULATE)` 4 TiB / 256 GiB. `escrypt_alloc_region` failure *is* covered safely with a 2^62-byte request (row 8.198).\n- **errors 8.155**: `pickparams` can never produce `r*p >= 2^30`; any other inner `_ll` failure needs a ≥64 GiB region.\n- The remaining 48 unreachable rows are genuine dead C branches on this platform (field already `uint32_t`, minimum of 0, `pickparams`/`escrypt_init_local` never failing, non-mmap fallback not compiled, dead enum values).\n\nOne incidental note: `tests/a1_randombytes_impl.rs` (area 1, not mine) failed once during a full-suite run while the shared cdylib was being rebuilt concurrently; it passes 5/5 in isolation and in later full runs.","usage":{"total_tokens":440152,"tool_uses":108,"duration_ms":3814294},"uuid":"470debb3-3fbc-4671-8866-810bcd17d1b5","session_id":"b566403e-4c11-4a9b-ad3a-d43b1f08afd2"}
