ws already annotated.\n\n## Tests added (`tests/a7_scalarmult_gaps.rs`, 10 tests)\nAll calls via `libloading`+`dlsym` on both `.so`s, fixed seeds, and every rejection checked against **four** distinct `q` pre-fill patterns so \"untouched\" is observable independently of the value that would have been written.\n\n- `gap_ref10_implementation_table` — the exported dispatch table (the 10th accessor of configs 7.28); differential `mult` / `mult_base`; wrapper-vs-primitive equivalence; `mult_base` unconditionally returns 0.\n- `gap_curve25519_base_never_fails` — the corpus (all-zero, all-`0xff`, `L`, `L-1`, `L+1`, `2L`, `7L`, `8L` truncated, `2^255-19`, `2^255`, `clamp(0)`, the 7 blocklist encodings *used as scalars*, + 400 random) × 4 pre-fills × both `_base` entry points: **rc is always 0, including `n = 0`**; plus `_base(n) == mult(n, basepoint)` cross-check and in-place `q == n`.\n- `gap_curve25519_blocklist_all_prefills` — 7 encodings × `|0x80` variants × 12 random scalars, early reject with `q` untouched on both `crypto_scalarmult_curve25519` and the generic alias.\n- `gap_curve25519_noncanonical_field_elements` — `p+2 … p+18` each proven equal to its reduction mod `p`; `2^255-1` vs `2^256-1`; real pk with bit 255 set.\n- `gap_ed25519_early_rejects_per_row` / `gap_ed25519_late_rejects_per_row` — errors 7.13–7.25 row by row, `q` compared C-vs-Rust byte for byte after each failure; early rejects leave `q` == pre-fill, late rejects hold the fully-written result (7.18 verified against `noclamp(clamp(0))`, 7.19/7.20/7.23/7.24 against `01 00 … 00`).\n- `gap_ristretto255_rejects_per_row` — errors 7.26–7.33, same treatment; identity point, 19 non-canonical encodings, 24 off-image canonical strings.\n- `gap_kx_vs_box_beforenm_consistency` (configs **7.129**) — 48 keypairs: kx session keys recomputed independently as `BLAKE2b-64(q ‖ cpk ‖ spk)`, `beforenm` recomputed as `HSalsa20(q, 0)`; both proven distinct from each other and from the raw DH secret, both stable, `beforenm` symmetric, and both failing on exactly the same 7 blocklist inputs with their outputs untouched.\n- `gap_build_configuration_invariants` (configs **7.130**) — observable consequences only: sandy2x symbols absent; `_pick_best_implementation` returns 0 and never changes a result; RFC 7748 vector correct (`fe25519_sub_lazy == fe25519_sub`); `S + L` **rejected** (a COMPAT build would accept it — the test asserts `sig[63] & 240 != 0` *and* `sig[63] & 224 == 0` to pin the discriminator), `S == L` and non-canonical `pk` rejected; signing bit-identical on repeat (`ED25519_NONDETERMINISTIC` off); `crypto_aead_aes256gcm_is_available() == 0`; ML-KEM implicit rejection reproducible across repeated calls and across C/Rust (`cmov` barrier absent).\n- `gap_accessors_are_constant_and_pure` — 8 size accessors × 8 calls, `crypto_scalarmult_primitive()` non-NULL and pointer-stable, generic aliases equal the curve25519 values.\n\n## Divergences\n**None.** `translation/src/` was not modified. Three initial red tests were all my own expectation bugs, and fixing them pinned down two genuine C subtleties now documented in the tests:\n1. `8L = 2^255 + 8c`, so the unconditional `t[31] &= 127` turns it into `8c`, which is *not* a multiple of `L` — so `n = 8L` is **accepted**, not rejected. Only `k ≤ 7` gives a genuine `_is_inf` rejection; the test now asserts both sides of that boundary.\n2. With `q == n` aliased and `n` all-zero, `unsigned char *t = q;` means the trailing `sodium_is_zero(n, 32)` reads the *freshly written output*, not the caller's scalar — so `crypto_scalarmult_ed25519` returns **0** there (clamped result is not the identity) while `_noclamp` still returns `-1` via `_is_inf(q)` alone.\n\n## `build-phaseA.sh` output\n`wrote ERRORS.md (1181 lines) and CONFIGS.md (1556 lines)`\n\nArea-7 row-count lines in the regenerated artifacts:\n- ERRORS.md: `| 7 | 129 |`\n- CONFIGS.md: `| 7 | 130 | 130 |` (totals now `| **total** | **1170** | **1157** |`)","usage":{"total_tokens":170375,"t