{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_sbcqab65pryyd4lgq6hjpwgg3ft6265vjvimapjd6te3ao7r6vkq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification complete. All four completion-gate conditions hold.\n\n## Results\n\n| Gate | Result |\n|---|---|\n| `SYMBOLS.md` — C symbols missing from Rust | **0** of 878 |\n| `SYMBOLS.md` — undefined non-libc symbols in Rust `.so` | **0** |\n| `CONFIGS.md` — Phase-B rows verified | **1157 `[x]` + 13 `[~]` of 1170** |\n| `ERRORS.md` — Phase-C rows with resolved status | **774 of 774** |\n| Feature combinations | **1 of 1** (crate declares no `[features]`) |\n| Tests | **614 passing, 0 failing** across 36 binaries, stable at `--test-threads` 1/2/3/4/6/8/16 |\n\n`c_src/` is untouched (all 341 source files still at checkout mtime).\n\n## Two real translation bugs found and fixed\n\n1. **`src/argon2_encoding.rs`** — `argon2_decode_string`/`argon2_encode_string` typed their `type` parameter as a 2-variant `#[repr(C)] enum` with an exhaustive `match`. C accepts any `int` there, so passing `0` materialized an invalid discriminant and took the wrong arm: decode returned `ARGON2_OK` where C returns `ARGON2_INCORRECT_TYPE` (-26), encode returned 0 where C returns `ARGON2_ENCODING_FAIL` (-31). Fixed by taking `c_int` and comparing numerically, propagating the plain `int` through the FFI boundary so an invalid enum is never formed. *This is exactly the out-of-range-enum class the brief called out.*\n\n2. **`src/blake2b.rs`** — the build defines no `NDEBUG`, so `crypto_generichash_blake2b_final`'s `assert(outlen <= UINT8_MAX)` is live. The port omitted it, so `outlen == 257` truncated to `1` and returned 0 where C dies on `SIGABRT`.\n\nEverything else in the ~51 kLOC library matched byte-for-byte, including opaque state images, `errno` values, and ~30 deliberately-preserved upstream quirks (the aes256gcm ENOSYS stub leaving out-lengths unwritten, the `crypto_kx` `tx == NULL` aliasing footgun, cofactored ed25519 verification, the `chacha20_ietf_xor_ic` guard underflow, `crypto_pwhash_str_alg` aborting instead of returning -1, secretstream's off-by-`sizeof` padding, …).\n\n## Three harness defects that had produced false divergences\n\nThe process-global deterministic RNG (now thread-local), the RNG-swapping tests racing each other (now mutexed), and a test that allocated a 32-byte BLAKE2b key while passing `keylen = 64` — reading heap garbage, which is why it failed only at `--test-threads=4`.\n\n## Artifacts in `translation/`\n\n`SYMBOLS.md`, `ERRORS.md`, `CONFIGS.md`, `VERIFICATION.md`, plus `check-symbols.sh` (Phase-D parity gate), `build-phaseA.sh` (regenerates the tables from `phaseA/`), and `run-all-features.sh` (derives the feature cross-product from `Cargo.toml`)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":446,"cache_read_input_tokens":420123,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":446,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b566403e-4c11-4a9b-ad3a-d43b1f08afd2","uuid":"20c1f3d8-51c1-4fd1-88db-a865ae4df53e","timestamp":"2026-08-31T05:52:42.831Z"}
